1
00:00:05,714 --> 00:00:06,924
[Sanghyun coughing]

2
00:00:08,634 --> 00:00:11,053
[continues coughing]

3
00:00:14,014 --> 00:00:15,140
[groans softly]

4
00:00:16,892 --> 00:00:17,935
It's so cold.

5
00:00:19,770 --> 00:00:23,357
It was so cold,
and I could hear water dripping.

6
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:27,152
I kept hearing water dripping,
and the mattress was too small for me.

7
00:00:27,236 --> 00:00:31,031
So I started thinking,
"I need to get out of here."

8
00:00:31,615 --> 00:00:34,868
Still, in a way,
it was a favorable situation for me.

9
00:00:35,619 --> 00:00:37,621
[♪ exhilarating music playing]

10
00:00:38,330 --> 00:00:41,291
The physical toll from the Main Match

11
00:00:41,375 --> 00:00:44,670
should definitely have an effect
on the others in the Death Match.

12
00:00:45,837 --> 00:00:48,465
Since I'm here in prison,
I can save up my energy.

13
00:00:48,549 --> 00:00:51,802
I'm going to wipe everyone out
and win the game.

14
00:00:51,885 --> 00:00:52,886
[grunts]

15
00:00:54,096 --> 00:00:55,138
I'm not worried.

16
00:00:56,390 --> 00:00:57,975
Finally. [sighs]

17
00:00:58,058 --> 00:00:59,268
PLAYERS WILL BE ELIMINATED
THROUGH DEATH MATCH

18
00:00:59,851 --> 00:01:01,228
I'm finally getting out.

19
00:01:01,311 --> 00:01:03,313
[♪ music fades]

20
00:01:03,939 --> 00:01:05,941
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

21
00:01:13,824 --> 00:01:14,825
[Ddolddol in English] What?

22
00:01:15,492 --> 00:01:16,994
-[Pani Bottle in Korean] What's this?
-[Eunsil sighs]

23
00:01:17,077 --> 00:01:18,078
[Ddolddol in English] Let's go.

24
00:01:18,161 --> 00:01:19,913
[Pani Bottle in Korean] Let's survive.
Let's unite, prison team.

25
00:01:19,997 --> 00:01:21,039
[Junseo] This is so scary.

26
00:01:21,123 --> 00:01:23,125
[♪ suspenseful music turns tense]

27
00:01:28,255 --> 00:01:32,968
[Sanghyun]
The team that I'd hoped would lose came.

28
00:01:33,051 --> 00:01:35,387
It was the team I wanted to face
in the Death Match.

29
00:01:35,470 --> 00:01:38,724
I was suspecting Jimin as the Seeker.

30
00:01:38,807 --> 00:01:41,810
I was hoping Jimin would be there.
And Ddolddol was there too,

31
00:01:41,893 --> 00:01:44,938
so it could be a good opportunity
to send them home.

32
00:01:45,022 --> 00:01:48,734
They say you always meet your enemies
in the Death Match. [chuckles]

33
00:01:48,817 --> 00:01:51,695
Sanghyun was unfairly sent to prison

34
00:01:51,778 --> 00:01:54,114
because I rallied everyone
to think he was the Seeker.

35
00:01:54,197 --> 00:01:56,491
Now, we've come face-to-face
in the Death Match.

36
00:01:56,575 --> 00:01:58,493
It was so awkward.

37
00:01:58,577 --> 00:02:01,204
Sanghyun, please forgive me this once.
I'm sorry.

38
00:02:01,288 --> 00:02:05,667
[Jimin] We laughed and cried together,
calling each other family.

39
00:02:05,751 --> 00:02:08,670
Now, we have to go up against one another
in the Death Match.

40
00:02:08,754 --> 00:02:09,963
[Junseo] It was exhausting. [exhales]

41
00:02:10,047 --> 00:02:12,841
[sighs] We had to become enemies
and compete against each other.

42
00:02:12,924 --> 00:02:16,261
[Eunsil] I didn't feel good about it,
but it's a Death Match, after all.

43
00:02:16,345 --> 00:02:18,388
I have to make it to the end.

44
00:02:18,472 --> 00:02:21,183
[Pani Bottle] I'd come this far,
so I hated the idea of leaving now.

45
00:02:21,266 --> 00:02:23,560
We had a solid strategy
for the last Death Match.

46
00:02:23,644 --> 00:02:25,687
We survived, so that was the right call.

47
00:02:25,771 --> 00:02:27,731
I'm going to do whatever I can.

48
00:02:27,814 --> 00:02:32,319
[host] We will now reveal
the second Death Match of Deadly Tag.

49
00:02:32,903 --> 00:02:35,405
The second Death Match of Deadly Tag is...

50
00:02:36,782 --> 00:02:38,075
"Old Money."

51
00:02:38,909 --> 00:02:40,952
"Old Money" is a game
with a set amount of cash

52
00:02:41,036 --> 00:02:43,121
that is used to earn points
through an auction

53
00:02:43,205 --> 00:02:46,041
and players must secure
both cash and points.

54
00:02:46,958 --> 00:02:48,126
[Jimin] An auction?

55
00:02:48,210 --> 00:02:50,253
[host] This game
is a six-player individual competition,

56
00:02:50,337 --> 00:02:54,299
and each player will start
with 200 million won in game money.

57
00:02:54,966 --> 00:02:57,094
The game consists of three rounds.

58
00:02:57,177 --> 00:03:01,056
Auction, Cash Round, and Auction.

59
00:03:01,139 --> 00:03:05,519
There will be six bids in Round 1
and five in Round 3.

60
00:03:05,602 --> 00:03:10,649
Auction items, inheritances,
and collections will appear at random.

61
00:03:10,732 --> 00:03:14,194
Auction items
are the main source of earning points,

62
00:03:14,277 --> 00:03:16,822
ranging from 1st to 10th Grade.

63
00:03:17,739 --> 00:03:20,575
Inheritances are items
that boost your score.

64
00:03:20,659 --> 00:03:24,121
Collections consist of items
that reduce your score.

65
00:03:24,955 --> 00:03:30,252
Auction items and inheritances
go to the highest bidder.

66
00:03:30,335 --> 00:03:31,586
WINNING BID

67
00:03:31,670 --> 00:03:35,966
Collections go to the first player
who drops out of bidding.

68
00:03:36,049 --> 00:03:37,134
OUT
COLLECTION ISSUED

69
00:03:37,217 --> 00:03:42,222
At this point, all players
must pay the amount of their final bid.

70
00:03:43,223 --> 00:03:47,102
In the Cash Round,
players find treasure to earn cash

71
00:03:47,185 --> 00:03:51,273
or tag other players to take their cash.

72
00:03:52,107 --> 00:03:55,110
If a player has no cash when tagged,

73
00:03:55,193 --> 00:03:58,405
one of their auction items or inheritances
will be taken by random.

74
00:03:58,488 --> 00:03:59,489
INHERITANCE ITEM

75
00:03:59,573 --> 00:04:03,368
If they have neither,
they will be eliminated.

76
00:04:03,452 --> 00:04:08,331
After the game, the final two eliminations
will be determined in the following order.

77
00:04:09,291 --> 00:04:12,711
First, the player with the lowest
auction score is eliminated.

78
00:04:12,794 --> 00:04:16,256
If two or more players are tied
for the lowest auction score,

79
00:04:16,339 --> 00:04:20,469
the player with the least
amount of cash is eliminated.

80
00:04:20,552 --> 00:04:23,930
Next, the player with the least
amount of cash among the remaining players

81
00:04:24,014 --> 00:04:25,640
is eliminated.

82
00:04:25,724 --> 00:04:28,810
If two or more players are tied
with the lowest amount of cash,

83
00:04:28,894 --> 00:04:32,439
the player with the lower
auction score is eliminated.

84
00:04:33,648 --> 00:04:37,611
The two selected players
will be eliminated from Deadly Tag.

85
00:04:38,111 --> 00:04:39,237
[Ddolddol sighs in exasperation]

86
00:04:39,321 --> 00:04:41,823
This is also a battle of wits.

87
00:04:41,907 --> 00:04:44,576
We take turns bidding on auctions,

88
00:04:44,659 --> 00:04:46,953
and you only get auction points
if your bid wins.

89
00:04:47,037 --> 00:04:48,997
So, of course,
it's about reading the others.

90
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:51,958
[Sanghyun] First, whoever
has the lowest score gets eliminated.

91
00:04:52,042 --> 00:04:55,295
Then, the next elimination
is based on how much money you have.

92
00:04:55,378 --> 00:04:57,214
[Pani Bottle] I think the key

93
00:04:57,297 --> 00:04:59,758
is keeping a good balance
between your score and cash.

94
00:04:59,841 --> 00:05:02,719
I just need to avoid being at the bottom
in either category.

95
00:05:02,803 --> 00:05:06,306
I'll try to stay somewhere in the middle
and play it safe.

96
00:05:06,890 --> 00:05:09,184
[dealer] We will begin the auction.

97
00:05:09,643 --> 00:05:13,271
FIRST AUCTION

98
00:05:13,355 --> 00:05:14,356
[exclaims]

99
00:05:15,065 --> 00:05:17,150
[dealer] We will unveil the auction item.

100
00:05:18,235 --> 00:05:19,444
[winces]

101
00:05:20,153 --> 00:05:21,238
Are you kidding me?

102
00:05:21,321 --> 00:05:22,864
[♪ music stops]

103
00:05:22,948 --> 00:05:23,990
[♪ comical music playing]

104
00:05:24,074 --> 00:05:25,534
MOMENTS AGO IN "KINGMAKER"

105
00:05:28,161 --> 00:05:31,289
ONE REASON FOR THE RED TEAM'S DEFEAT

106
00:05:31,373 --> 00:05:33,959
FIRST ITEM: THE LOVE-HATE SYMBOL

107
00:05:35,669 --> 00:05:37,462
[sighs, winces]

108
00:05:37,546 --> 00:05:39,589
SICK AND TIRED OF THEM

109
00:05:39,673 --> 00:05:44,469
[dealer] This auction item
is the 8th Grade item, "Symbol."

110
00:05:44,553 --> 00:05:47,764
The winning bid will receive three points.

111
00:05:47,848 --> 00:05:50,058
We'll start the bidding
with Mr. Youn Sanghyun.

112
00:05:50,141 --> 00:05:51,518
STARTING WITH PLAYER WITH MOST FUNDS

113
00:05:51,601 --> 00:05:53,603
-Please state your bid.
-One million won.

114
00:05:53,687 --> 00:05:55,146
-Two million.
-Three million.

115
00:05:55,230 --> 00:05:56,481
[Jimin] Five million.

116
00:05:57,023 --> 00:05:58,817
-[dealer] Okay, Mr. Kim Ddolddol?
-Seven million.

117
00:05:58,900 --> 00:06:00,902
[♪ intriguing music plays]

118
00:06:03,238 --> 00:06:04,447
-I bid 21 million.
-[♪ music stops]

119
00:06:04,531 --> 00:06:06,366
[dealer] We have 21 million won.

120
00:06:06,449 --> 00:06:08,034
FLUSTERED

121
00:06:08,118 --> 00:06:10,120
-I'm out.
-I'm out.

122
00:06:10,203 --> 00:06:11,246
I'm out.

123
00:06:12,038 --> 00:06:13,081
[dealer] Mr. Kim Ddolddol.

124
00:06:13,832 --> 00:06:14,875
I bid 26 million.

125
00:06:14,958 --> 00:06:16,793
[dealer] We have 26 million won.
Mr. Pani Bottle?

126
00:06:16,877 --> 00:06:18,920
[♪ tense music playing]

127
00:06:19,004 --> 00:06:20,213
I'm out.

128
00:06:20,297 --> 00:06:21,423
[dealer] Mr. Pani Bottle is out.

129
00:06:21,506 --> 00:06:25,969
Sold to Mr. Kim Ddolddol
for 26 million won.

130
00:06:26,052 --> 00:06:28,805
[Ddolddol] I thought
the most important thing in this round

131
00:06:28,889 --> 00:06:30,849
was to win an auction item.

132
00:06:30,932 --> 00:06:34,227
I figured 30 million won was fair
for three points.

133
00:06:34,311 --> 00:06:35,520
It was pretty good.

134
00:06:35,604 --> 00:06:38,189
-[♪ tense music continues playing]
-[sighs heavily]

135
00:06:39,149 --> 00:06:42,402
[dealer] The second auction item
is a 4th Grade item.

136
00:06:42,485 --> 00:06:45,322
The winning bid will receive seven points.

137
00:06:46,448 --> 00:06:47,490
I bid 30 million.

138
00:06:47,574 --> 00:06:50,118
[dealer] We have 30 million won.

139
00:06:50,201 --> 00:06:51,536
I bid 60 million.

140
00:06:51,620 --> 00:06:52,996
I'm out.

141
00:06:53,079 --> 00:06:55,290
-[Ddolddol] I'm out.
-I'm out.

142
00:06:55,373 --> 00:06:56,666
[dealer] Mr. Yuk Junseo.

143
00:06:57,459 --> 00:06:58,752
I bid 70 million.

144
00:06:58,835 --> 00:07:00,337
[dealer] We have 70 million won.

145
00:07:02,172 --> 00:07:03,256
Mr. Pani Bottle.

146
00:07:04,466 --> 00:07:05,925
I'm out. [sighs]

147
00:07:06,009 --> 00:07:08,261
-I'm out.
-[dealer] Ms. Jang Eunsil is out.

148
00:07:08,803 --> 00:07:11,931
This auction item goes to Mr. Yuk Junseo.

149
00:07:12,015 --> 00:07:13,224
ROUND 1, AUCTION 2
PLUS 7 POINTS

150
00:07:13,808 --> 00:07:16,561
[Ddolddol] I spent 26 million won
to get three points,

151
00:07:16,645 --> 00:07:19,606
while Junseo spent 70 million won
to get seven points.

152
00:07:19,689 --> 00:07:23,234
I think I got a slightly better deal.

153
00:07:23,318 --> 00:07:25,403
[dealer] We will unveil the auction item.

154
00:07:26,363 --> 00:07:27,364
It's something different.

155
00:07:28,323 --> 00:07:29,449
What is it?

156
00:07:29,532 --> 00:07:34,245
[dealer] This auction item
is a collection for negative five points.

157
00:07:34,329 --> 00:07:36,122
It will take away five points.

158
00:07:36,206 --> 00:07:37,666
[♪ tense music turns suspenseful]

159
00:07:37,749 --> 00:07:40,293
So you're basically
trading money for points.

160
00:07:41,419 --> 00:07:43,088
This one's going to take a while.

161
00:07:43,880 --> 00:07:46,883
I figured everyone would spend
pretty much the same amount,

162
00:07:46,966 --> 00:07:50,178
so I decided to keep bidding
without folding at all.

163
00:07:50,261 --> 00:07:52,180
Why the hell did a collection come up?

164
00:07:53,014 --> 00:07:56,226
I'd decided I had to avoid collections.

165
00:07:56,309 --> 00:08:00,772
Starting off with negative points
would make it more likely that I'd lose.

166
00:08:00,855 --> 00:08:03,066
[Ddolddol]
This is basically a game of chicken.

167
00:08:03,149 --> 00:08:08,029
[dealer] By the way, formula-related items
do not apply basic arithmetic.

168
00:08:08,113 --> 00:08:11,408
Items must be used
in the order they were acquired.

169
00:08:11,491 --> 00:08:13,284
That means there's multiplication.

170
00:08:13,368 --> 00:08:15,328
-There's multiplication and division.
-[Ddolddol] What?

171
00:08:15,412 --> 00:08:16,705
[♪ pensive music playing]

172
00:08:16,788 --> 00:08:18,456
Okay, we will begin the auction.

173
00:08:18,540 --> 00:08:21,626
We will begin with Mr. Yuk Junseo.
Please state your bid.

174
00:08:21,710 --> 00:08:22,919
I bid 10 million.

175
00:08:23,002 --> 00:08:24,087
I bid 12 million.

176
00:08:24,170 --> 00:08:25,380
I bid 13 million.

177
00:08:25,463 --> 00:08:27,048
[sighs] I bid 14 million.

178
00:08:27,590 --> 00:08:29,050
I bid 40 million.

179
00:08:30,135 --> 00:08:32,804
THE BIDS SHOOT UP IN SECONDS

180
00:08:32,887 --> 00:08:34,305
[Junseo] What is going on?

181
00:08:34,389 --> 00:08:37,642
I was keeping track of how much money
everyone else had spent.

182
00:08:37,726 --> 00:08:40,395
And Junseo had spent a lot of money,

183
00:08:40,478 --> 00:08:43,189
so I figured
I'd drive up the price on him.

184
00:08:43,273 --> 00:08:44,524
I bid 41 million.

185
00:08:44,607 --> 00:08:46,901
-I bid 42 million.
-I bid 43 million.

186
00:08:46,985 --> 00:08:48,069
I bid 44 million.

187
00:08:48,153 --> 00:08:49,946
[dealer] We have 44 million.
Mr. Pani Bottle.

188
00:08:50,030 --> 00:08:53,033
[breathes deeply]

189
00:08:53,116 --> 00:08:55,118
[♪ pensive music continues playing]

190
00:09:00,957 --> 00:09:02,709
[dealer] Mr. Pani Bottle, time is...

191
00:09:03,877 --> 00:09:04,878
-I'm out.
-[♪ music stops]

192
00:09:05,920 --> 00:09:08,840
[Sanghyun] Wait,
he's giving up earlier than I expected.

193
00:09:09,424 --> 00:09:10,425
[Junseo] I was relieved.

194
00:09:11,342 --> 00:09:13,803
[dealer] Mr. Pani Bottle has dropped out.

195
00:09:13,887 --> 00:09:19,517
Everyone else
must pay your current final bids.

196
00:09:19,601 --> 00:09:21,603
[♪ tense music playing]

197
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:26,941
[Pani Bottle] For one thing,

198
00:09:27,025 --> 00:09:29,319
I thought the price
was way too high for the points.

199
00:09:29,402 --> 00:09:33,364
And I figured
there would be something better later on.

200
00:09:33,448 --> 00:09:34,449
[sighs heavily]

201
00:09:34,532 --> 00:09:38,119
PANI BOTTLE HOLDS BACK
BIG SPENDING FOR LATER

202
00:09:38,203 --> 00:09:40,121
AUCTION STATUS
1ST: YUK JUNSEO, 7 POINTS

203
00:09:40,205 --> 00:09:42,207
1ST: PANI BOTTLE, 164 MILLION WON

204
00:09:42,290 --> 00:09:44,918
PANI BOTTLE, YUK JUNSEO
IN DANGER OF ELIMINATION

205
00:09:45,001 --> 00:09:46,586
[dealer] We will unveil the auction item.

206
00:09:47,337 --> 00:09:48,463
[gasps]

207
00:09:48,546 --> 00:09:51,091
Oh, my gosh! I want that. [giggles]

208
00:09:52,008 --> 00:09:55,762
[dealer] The 1st Grade item,
"Blue Eye of the Ocean."

209
00:09:56,930 --> 00:09:59,849
The winning bid will receive 10 points.

210
00:09:59,933 --> 00:10:01,142
-[exclaims]
-[♪ lively music playing]

211
00:10:01,226 --> 00:10:04,312
[Sanghyun] Since the most is 10 points,
I figured everyone would fight for it.

212
00:10:04,395 --> 00:10:07,190
So early on,
I set my limit at about 80 million.

213
00:10:07,273 --> 00:10:09,109
I'd go as high as 80 million won.

214
00:10:09,192 --> 00:10:11,569
[groans] Let me have this one, please.

215
00:10:11,653 --> 00:10:13,822
I was determined to get it on my turn.

216
00:10:13,905 --> 00:10:15,657
[dealer] Mr. Pani Bottle,
please state your bid.

217
00:10:15,740 --> 00:10:17,158
[inhales sharply]

218
00:10:17,242 --> 00:10:21,121
Let's see. I bid 50 million won.

219
00:10:21,704 --> 00:10:24,707
[dealer] We have a bid of 50 million won.
Mr. Youn Sanghyun?

220
00:10:25,667 --> 00:10:27,418
-I bid 51 million.
-[dealer] We have 51 million.

221
00:10:27,502 --> 00:10:28,670
I bid 52 million.

222
00:10:28,753 --> 00:10:29,879
I bid 56 million.

223
00:10:29,963 --> 00:10:31,047
[Pani Bottle] I bid 60 million.

224
00:10:31,131 --> 00:10:32,340
I bid 70 million.

225
00:10:32,423 --> 00:10:33,466
I bid 80 million.

226
00:10:33,967 --> 00:10:35,009
I'm out.

227
00:10:35,593 --> 00:10:37,220
I am out.

228
00:10:37,303 --> 00:10:38,429
[Ddolddol] I'm out.

229
00:10:38,513 --> 00:10:39,764
[dealer] Mr. Kim Ddolddol has dropped out.

230
00:10:39,848 --> 00:10:42,767
[Sanghyun]
My original limit was 80 million.

231
00:10:42,851 --> 00:10:45,228
The moment it passed that point,
I was ready to bow out.

232
00:10:45,311 --> 00:10:46,312
I bid 90 million.

233
00:10:46,938 --> 00:10:48,022
[dealer] We have 90 million won.

234
00:10:48,106 --> 00:10:49,190
I bid 92 million.

235
00:10:49,274 --> 00:10:50,316
I'm out.

236
00:10:50,400 --> 00:10:51,985
[dealer] Mr. Pani Bottle has dropped out.

237
00:10:52,068 --> 00:10:53,945
IT'S DOWN TO YOUN SANGHYUN AND JANG EUNSIL

238
00:10:54,028 --> 00:10:55,029
I bid 100 million.

239
00:10:55,113 --> 00:10:56,698
[dealer]
Mr. Youn Sanghyun bids 100 million won.

240
00:10:57,240 --> 00:10:58,283
I bid 110 million.

241
00:10:58,366 --> 00:10:59,617
[dealer] We have 110 million won.

242
00:11:00,410 --> 00:11:03,746
[Sanghyun]
I know Eunsil is really competitive.

243
00:11:03,872 --> 00:11:07,417
I expected her to keep up
with whatever I bid.

244
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:10,378
When I bid 100 million won,
she immediately matched it,

245
00:11:10,461 --> 00:11:12,297
so I decided to pump it up a bit
and drop out.

246
00:11:12,380 --> 00:11:14,257
-[dealer] Mr. Youn Sanghyun.
-I bid 112 million.

247
00:11:14,340 --> 00:11:15,884
-[dealer] We have 112 million.
-[Jimin laughs]

248
00:11:15,967 --> 00:11:17,719
-[Jimin] This is killing me.
-[dealer] Ms. Jang Eunsil.

249
00:11:17,802 --> 00:11:21,181
[Eunsil]
I thought the price wasn't too bad.

250
00:11:21,264 --> 00:11:23,266
I bid 114 million!

251
00:11:23,349 --> 00:11:25,435
[dealer] We have 114 million won.

252
00:11:25,518 --> 00:11:26,978
[Eunsil]
I felt like I had to keep pushing.

253
00:11:27,061 --> 00:11:28,354
My competitive side kicked in.

254
00:11:28,438 --> 00:11:30,064
-[dealer] Mr. Youn Sanghyun...
-[Jimin] This is so damn funny.

255
00:11:30,148 --> 00:11:31,482
I bid 116 million!

256
00:11:31,566 --> 00:11:33,234
[Jimin] Has he lost his damn mind?

257
00:11:33,860 --> 00:11:36,946
[dealer] We have 116 million won.
Ms. Jang Eunsil.

258
00:11:37,030 --> 00:11:38,156
I bid 120 million.

259
00:11:38,239 --> 00:11:39,365
[exclaims]

260
00:11:39,449 --> 00:11:41,701
-[dealer] We have 120 million won.
-I'm out!

261
00:11:41,784 --> 00:11:46,164
[dealer] Sold to Ms. Jang Eunsil
for 120 million won.

262
00:11:46,247 --> 00:11:47,457
-This is insane.
-[Ddolddol exclaims]

263
00:11:48,917 --> 00:11:50,793
[Sanghyun] I felt pretty proud.

264
00:11:50,877 --> 00:11:53,922
After all, the person
with the lowest score gets eliminated.

265
00:11:54,005 --> 00:11:56,049
You don't need to spend big
on a 1st Grade item.

266
00:11:56,633 --> 00:11:59,010
[Eunsil] I decided to take
the 10-point item and wait it out.

267
00:11:59,093 --> 00:12:03,890
I planned to survive all the rounds
with the cash I had and this necklace.

268
00:12:03,973 --> 00:12:05,850
[dealer] We will move on to the next item.

269
00:12:05,934 --> 00:12:08,937
This auction item is the 5th Grade item,

270
00:12:09,020 --> 00:12:11,231
Prisoners' Round.

271
00:12:11,314 --> 00:12:13,066
The winning bid will receive six points.

272
00:12:13,608 --> 00:12:14,901
Please state your bid.

273
00:12:15,401 --> 00:12:17,362
-I bid 50 million.
-[dealer] We have 50 million won.

274
00:12:17,987 --> 00:12:19,697
Fifty million... I'm out.

275
00:12:19,781 --> 00:12:21,074
I'm out.

276
00:12:21,157 --> 00:12:24,577
[dealer] Sold to Mr. Kim Ddolddol
for 50 million won.

277
00:12:24,661 --> 00:12:25,828
ROUND 1, AUCTION 5
PLUS 6 POINTS

278
00:12:25,912 --> 00:12:27,872
[Ddolddol]
I had one of the highest scores.

279
00:12:27,956 --> 00:12:30,917
I think I did a really good job
in the first auction round.

280
00:12:31,709 --> 00:12:33,670
AUCTION STATUS
1ST: JANG EUNSIL, 10 POINTS

281
00:12:33,753 --> 00:12:35,713
1ST: PANI BOTTLE, 164 MILLION WON

282
00:12:35,797 --> 00:12:38,424
PANI BOTTLE AND JANG EUNSIL
IN DANGER OF ELIMINATION

283
00:12:38,508 --> 00:12:39,884
[dealer]
The final auction item for Round 1.

284
00:12:39,968 --> 00:12:41,469
LAST ROUND 1 AUCTION IS BLIND AUCTION

285
00:12:41,552 --> 00:12:43,805
The 7th Grade item, The Night Watch.

286
00:12:43,888 --> 00:12:46,557
The winning bid will receive four points.

287
00:12:47,976 --> 00:12:50,979
[Pani Bottle]
I'm currently at minus five points,

288
00:12:51,062 --> 00:12:53,022
so I really need those four points.

289
00:12:53,106 --> 00:12:56,025
I set my bid high enough
to make sure I got it.

290
00:12:56,109 --> 00:12:57,443
PANI BOTTLE SPENDS NEARLY HALF HIS MONEY

291
00:12:57,777 --> 00:12:58,778
[♪ tense music playing]

292
00:12:58,861 --> 00:13:00,238
[dealer] Thank you, Mr. Pani Bottle.

293
00:13:00,822 --> 00:13:03,241
[Jimin] Since I was low on points,

294
00:13:03,324 --> 00:13:06,703
I knew I had to get this one,
so I spent a lot of money on it.

295
00:13:06,786 --> 00:13:08,871
[Sanghyun mumbles]

296
00:13:08,955 --> 00:13:12,333
I wanted to secure the points
and stay safe,

297
00:13:12,417 --> 00:13:14,210
so I decided to bid a bit higher.

298
00:13:15,044 --> 00:13:17,672
BLIND AUCTION ENDS

299
00:13:17,755 --> 00:13:20,925
[dealer]
We have determined the winning bidder.

300
00:13:21,592 --> 00:13:23,594
[♪ suspenseful music plays]

301
00:13:25,221 --> 00:13:28,433
The final winning bid is 101 million won.

302
00:13:29,392 --> 00:13:32,562
[Pani Bottle] Wow.
When I heard the price, I thought,

303
00:13:32,645 --> 00:13:35,648
"I was way short." I was so disappointed.

304
00:13:35,732 --> 00:13:38,526
-[♪ exhilarating music playing]
-[exclaims, snorts]

305
00:13:38,609 --> 00:13:41,029
I was going to spend 80 million,
but I spent 100 million.

306
00:13:41,112 --> 00:13:42,238
I spent 101 million won.

307
00:13:42,321 --> 00:13:44,991
I knew I'd reached a bit too far.

308
00:13:45,074 --> 00:13:46,826
[dealer] The auction is now closed.

309
00:13:47,535 --> 00:13:49,662
ROUND 1 AUCTION RESULTS
1ST: JANG EUNSIL, 10 POINTS

310
00:13:49,746 --> 00:13:51,539
2ND: PARK JIMIN, 157 MILLION WON

311
00:13:51,622 --> 00:13:54,250
PANI BOTTLE AND JANG EUNSIL
IN DANGER OF ELIMINATION

312
00:13:54,333 --> 00:13:58,087
[host] We will now begin Round 2,
the Cash Round.

313
00:13:58,629 --> 00:14:02,216
In the Cash Round, you can tag
other players to take their cash

314
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:05,803
or find hidden treasure to earn cash.

315
00:14:06,554 --> 00:14:08,056
The Cash Round area consists of

316
00:14:08,139 --> 00:14:10,058
the Shopping Arcade,

317
00:14:10,141 --> 00:14:12,101
the Grand Mansion,

318
00:14:12,185 --> 00:14:14,520
and the Wasteland.

319
00:14:14,604 --> 00:14:16,939
There is a Black Market
in the Shopping Arcade.

320
00:14:17,023 --> 00:14:18,024
[♪ tense music builds]

321
00:14:18,107 --> 00:14:21,736
The Black Market has a menu
with hidden treasure information.

322
00:14:21,819 --> 00:14:23,321
BLACK MARKET
NOW BUYING

323
00:14:23,404 --> 00:14:26,783
Three hidden treasures can be found
in the Grand Mansion and Wasteland

324
00:14:26,866 --> 00:14:28,826
and can be sold at the Black Market.

325
00:14:29,911 --> 00:14:33,956
Build your wealth by looting treasure
or stealing from other players.

326
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:38,294
[Sanghyun]
I was dead set on finding treasure.

327
00:14:38,377 --> 00:14:39,796
[♪ music intensifies]

328
00:14:39,879 --> 00:14:42,632
GRAND MANSION, AUCTION HOUSE
WASTELAND, SHOPPING ARCADE

329
00:14:43,257 --> 00:14:48,805
PLAYERS START SEARCHING FOR TREASURE

330
00:14:49,430 --> 00:14:50,515
Where is it?

331
00:14:51,641 --> 00:14:53,267
[Pani Bottle] Can we talk for a second?

332
00:14:53,351 --> 00:14:54,393
[whispering] Help me out just this once.

333
00:14:54,477 --> 00:14:55,561
[Ddolddol] How much do you have left?

334
00:14:55,645 --> 00:14:57,105
I just did the math.

335
00:14:57,188 --> 00:14:58,856
-I have about 100 million.
-Okay.

336
00:14:58,940 --> 00:15:01,859
Eunsil's at the bottom with 39 million.

337
00:15:01,943 --> 00:15:03,778
As long as we stay above that,
we're safe.

338
00:15:03,861 --> 00:15:04,862
[Ddolddol] Right.

339
00:15:04,946 --> 00:15:06,739
I'm on your side
since we were fellow inmates.

340
00:15:06,823 --> 00:15:07,824
PRISON ALLIANCE REUNITES

341
00:15:07,907 --> 00:15:11,828
It's a big advantage for me
to be safe around Ddolddol.

342
00:15:11,911 --> 00:15:15,456
Now, he can fully back me up.

343
00:15:16,082 --> 00:15:17,792
[Ddolddol] We need to find treasure.

344
00:15:19,961 --> 00:15:22,672
[Pani Bottle] Since there was a risk
of getting tagged while walking around,

345
00:15:22,755 --> 00:15:25,383
I thought I'd put my patch on my back

346
00:15:25,466 --> 00:15:29,220
and pretend I was on my way
to the Dealer Room after getting tagged.

347
00:15:29,303 --> 00:15:31,139
That way, I could move around safely,

348
00:15:31,222 --> 00:15:32,598
and that's the idea I came up with.

349
00:15:32,682 --> 00:15:34,350
[Ddolddol] It's as if I betrayed you...

350
00:15:34,433 --> 00:15:36,602
You need to look bummed
as if I betrayed you.

351
00:15:36,686 --> 00:15:38,521
[♪ quirky music plays]

352
00:15:38,604 --> 00:15:40,439
-[Junseo exclaims]
-[Ddolddol] Can you believe this?

353
00:15:41,023 --> 00:15:43,442
-[Junseo exclaims]
-[♪ quirky music turns intriguing]

354
00:15:43,526 --> 00:15:46,445
[Ddolddol] Just five to 10 minutes in,
he suddenly showed up.

355
00:15:49,365 --> 00:15:50,825
[Pani Bottle] I got caught.

356
00:15:50,908 --> 00:15:52,952
[Ddolddol] Where's the Dealer Room?

357
00:15:53,035 --> 00:15:55,621
[Junseo] It's upstairs.
Go up and all the way to the left.

358
00:15:55,705 --> 00:15:57,748
I thought you two
would never tag each other...

359
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:00,334
FAKE TAG TRICK WORKED

360
00:16:00,418 --> 00:16:01,669
[Pani Bottle whispering]
I told you it'd work.

361
00:16:02,920 --> 00:16:05,131
-I'll cover you, so can you go find them?
-Okay.

362
00:16:05,214 --> 00:16:07,967
How do you know what's treasure?
Can you tell right away?

363
00:16:08,050 --> 00:16:09,886
[Ddolddol] Lift that helmet. Just in case.

364
00:16:10,761 --> 00:16:11,762
[Pani Bottle] Helmet?

365
00:16:13,181 --> 00:16:14,265
God damn it.

366
00:16:15,099 --> 00:16:16,434
[sighs]

367
00:16:16,517 --> 00:16:17,518
[Ddolddol whispering] Nothing?

368
00:16:17,602 --> 00:16:18,853
[Pani Bottle]
It looks like there's nothing.

369
00:16:19,395 --> 00:16:21,147
They said we have to go
to the Black Market

370
00:16:21,230 --> 00:16:23,941
to know what they look like
and how much they're worth.

371
00:16:24,775 --> 00:16:27,153
This is like
finding a needle in a haystack.

372
00:16:27,737 --> 00:16:31,532
MEANWHILE, YOUN SANGHYUN
LOOKS FOR THE BLACK MARKET

373
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:34,035
SHOPPING ARCADE BLACK MARKET

374
00:16:34,118 --> 00:16:36,370
[Sanghyun] I went to the Black Market
and checked first.

375
00:16:36,954 --> 00:16:38,664
BLACK MARKET MENU
IN FRONT OF DEALER ROOM

376
00:16:38,748 --> 00:16:42,293
BLACK MARKET: NOW BUYING
PLASTER STATUE, LARGE PAINTING, VASE

377
00:16:42,376 --> 00:16:44,128
[whispering] A plaster statue,
a large painting...

378
00:16:45,213 --> 00:16:48,049
I saw it and realized,
"These are bigger than I thought."

379
00:16:48,132 --> 00:16:51,177
THE TREASURES ARE LARGE IN SIZE

380
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:53,012
It would be hard to hide these.

381
00:16:53,095 --> 00:16:55,806
So, I went straight to the Wasteland.

382
00:16:55,890 --> 00:16:58,017
And I started searching through the cars.

383
00:16:58,601 --> 00:17:00,561
I think a large painting would be here.

384
00:17:02,104 --> 00:17:03,105
Where is it?

385
00:17:03,189 --> 00:17:05,399
[♪ exhilarating music playing]

386
00:17:05,983 --> 00:17:08,069
It's got to be here. Why can't I find it?

387
00:17:12,281 --> 00:17:13,449
[Junseo] A large painting and a vase?

388
00:17:13,532 --> 00:17:15,284
AT THAT MOMENT,
JUNSEO CHECKS MENU

389
00:17:16,118 --> 00:17:17,161
[whispering] A plaster statue...

390
00:17:23,292 --> 00:17:24,293
[Sanghyun] A vase...

391
00:17:29,215 --> 00:17:30,341
[Junseo] This can't be it.

392
00:17:32,510 --> 00:17:35,221
Geez, there's nothing.

393
00:17:36,639 --> 00:17:40,726
[Sanghyun] I just couldn't find anything,
and when I turned around,

394
00:17:40,810 --> 00:17:42,687
the plaster statue
was right in front of me.

395
00:17:42,770 --> 00:17:45,106
So, I just snatched it
without saying a word,

396
00:17:45,189 --> 00:17:46,691
and I sprinted off.

397
00:17:47,358 --> 00:17:49,986
CASH ROUND
ALARM GOES OFF WHEN AN ITEM IS STOLEN

398
00:17:50,069 --> 00:17:51,737
[alarm blaring]

399
00:17:51,821 --> 00:17:52,822
[Ddolddol] What's that sound?

400
00:17:52,905 --> 00:17:54,156
[Pani Bottle] It's the treasure.

401
00:17:54,240 --> 00:17:55,241
Someone stole one.

402
00:17:56,784 --> 00:17:57,785
[Junseo] Who is it?

403
00:17:57,868 --> 00:17:58,869
[alarm stops blaring]

404
00:18:00,288 --> 00:18:03,082
[dealer] Hello, Mr. Youn Sanghyun.

405
00:18:03,165 --> 00:18:04,959
We will check your item.

406
00:18:07,128 --> 00:18:09,547
It matches an item
the Black Market is buying.

407
00:18:09,630 --> 00:18:12,508
You have been awarded
50 million won in cash.

408
00:18:12,592 --> 00:18:15,136
[Sanghyun]
That's how I scored 50 million won.

409
00:18:15,219 --> 00:18:16,554
5TH: SANGHYUN, 59 MILLION WON

410
00:18:16,637 --> 00:18:17,805
3RD: SANGHYUN, 109 MILLION WON

411
00:18:17,888 --> 00:18:21,934
PANI BOTTLE AND JANG EUNSIL
IN DANGER OF ELIMINATION

412
00:18:22,018 --> 00:18:23,019
[whispering] Are there any more?

413
00:18:23,102 --> 00:18:24,395
SANGHYUN ESCAPES FINANCIAL TROUBLE

414
00:18:24,478 --> 00:18:25,813
A large painting and a vase.

415
00:18:25,896 --> 00:18:28,524
After I found the plaster statue
and got distracted by money,

416
00:18:28,608 --> 00:18:30,735
I decided I had to find
all the other items.

417
00:18:30,818 --> 00:18:33,904
I don't think they hid them that well.

418
00:18:33,988 --> 00:18:38,326
They should be
just sitting out in the open.

419
00:18:40,244 --> 00:18:43,289
I saw this little crawl space,
so I checked it out.

420
00:18:45,374 --> 00:18:46,751
And it was right there.

421
00:18:48,878 --> 00:18:50,713
I found a vase on the first floor.

422
00:18:52,381 --> 00:18:53,424
[alarm blaring]

423
00:18:53,507 --> 00:18:55,968
And as soon as I grabbed it,
the alarm went off.

424
00:18:56,052 --> 00:18:57,470
So, I ran as fast as I could.

425
00:18:59,805 --> 00:19:01,474
[Pani Bottle]
Someone must have found treasure.

426
00:19:02,975 --> 00:19:06,604
[Sanghyun] All I could think was,
"Just run to the Black Market."

427
00:19:06,687 --> 00:19:08,689
[♪ exhilarating music playing]

428
00:19:09,690 --> 00:19:11,025
[Pani Bottle] He found it.
He found treasure.

429
00:19:11,108 --> 00:19:12,943
How did he find it?

430
00:19:13,027 --> 00:19:15,696
[Sanghyun panting]

431
00:19:15,780 --> 00:19:19,283
[dealer] It matches an item
the Black Market is buying.

432
00:19:19,367 --> 00:19:21,077
Here is 20 million won.

433
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:22,161
VASE
20 MILLION WON

434
00:19:22,244 --> 00:19:26,082
I guess I got good rest in prison.
I gladly walked away with the money.

435
00:19:30,002 --> 00:19:32,755
[host] The Cash Round is over.

436
00:19:32,838 --> 00:19:34,590
[♪ music stops]

437
00:19:34,674 --> 00:19:36,550
CASH ROUND RESULTS
1ST: JANG EUNSIL, 10 POINTS

438
00:19:36,634 --> 00:19:38,552
3RD: YOUN SANGHYUN, 129 MILLION WON

439
00:19:38,636 --> 00:19:41,389
PANI BOTTLE AND JANG EUNSIL
IN DANGER OF ELIMINATION

440
00:19:42,556 --> 00:19:44,100
[Jimin huffs]

441
00:19:45,393 --> 00:19:47,895
-[♪ suspenseful music playing]
-[Pani Bottle clears throat]

442
00:19:48,896 --> 00:19:50,439
-[Ddolddol] We're back.
-[Pani Bottle] Sanghyun.

443
00:19:50,523 --> 00:19:52,066
-[Sanghyun] Yes?
-[Pani Bottle] Can we talk for a second?

444
00:19:52,566 --> 00:19:53,693
[Sanghyun] Talk? Right now?

445
00:19:56,404 --> 00:19:57,655
[Pani Bottle whispering]
You found treasure, right?

446
00:19:57,738 --> 00:19:59,448
-[Sanghyun] Me? Yes.
-[Pani Bottle] I saw you.

447
00:20:01,617 --> 00:20:03,202
Please do me a favor.

448
00:20:03,285 --> 00:20:05,621
Now, I'm not a threat to you anyway.

449
00:20:06,539 --> 00:20:09,208
-I'm trailing by a lot right now.
-[Sanghyun] Right.

450
00:20:09,291 --> 00:20:12,670
[Pani Bottle]
If a "divide by two" collection comes up,

451
00:20:12,753 --> 00:20:14,922
I'm definitely going to go for it.

452
00:20:15,506 --> 00:20:16,507
BACK IN ROUND 2

453
00:20:16,590 --> 00:20:17,591
[sighs] I'm in a lot of danger.

454
00:20:17,675 --> 00:20:19,885
[Ddolddol] Your score.
You really need to take

455
00:20:19,969 --> 00:20:22,096
a good amount of points in the auction.

456
00:20:22,179 --> 00:20:23,222
If...

457
00:20:23,305 --> 00:20:25,307
[♪ pensive music playing]

458
00:20:26,726 --> 00:20:28,394
..."divide by two" comes up...

459
00:20:28,477 --> 00:20:30,896
Listen. Collections do no good.

460
00:20:31,397 --> 00:20:33,691
So "times by" won't be good, right?

461
00:20:33,774 --> 00:20:35,359
They mentioned arithmetic operations.

462
00:20:35,443 --> 00:20:36,444
EXPECTING DIVISION TO APPEAR

463
00:20:36,527 --> 00:20:39,196
If there were only plus and minus,
why even mention that?

464
00:20:39,280 --> 00:20:41,699
It's division. There has to be division.

465
00:20:41,782 --> 00:20:44,702
So, everyone else is going to avoid it,
and when it's my turn,

466
00:20:44,785 --> 00:20:47,204
I'll have to take it.
That puts me at minus 2.5.

467
00:20:47,830 --> 00:20:49,165
[whispering]
If I take the "divide by two,"

468
00:20:49,248 --> 00:20:50,791
I'll be at minus 2.5.

469
00:20:50,875 --> 00:20:52,918
After that, I need to take a big one.

470
00:20:53,002 --> 00:20:55,004
If a 10-point item comes up,
I have a shot

471
00:20:55,087 --> 00:20:56,380
if I can get those 10 points.

472
00:20:56,464 --> 00:20:58,924
So, don't run up the bids too high.
Please let me have it.

473
00:20:59,008 --> 00:21:00,885
That's all I'm asking for.

474
00:21:00,968 --> 00:21:02,511
-Jimin.
-[Jimin] Yeah?

475
00:21:03,179 --> 00:21:05,306
[whispering] If your score ends up

476
00:21:05,389 --> 00:21:07,266
-higher than Junseo's...
-[Jimin] Yeah.

477
00:21:07,349 --> 00:21:10,269
...could you let me have the 10-point item
when it comes up?

478
00:21:10,352 --> 00:21:11,353
I had nothing to lose.

479
00:21:11,437 --> 00:21:13,689
If I have to play dirty
to move up, then I will.

480
00:21:13,773 --> 00:21:15,691
Even if it's dirty,
let's do what it takes.

481
00:21:16,275 --> 00:21:17,276
[whispering] I'll see what I can do.

482
00:21:18,527 --> 00:21:20,738
Pani Bottle kept asking me
to help him out.

483
00:21:20,821 --> 00:21:22,156
He asked Sanghyun as well.

484
00:21:22,239 --> 00:21:25,242
But if I did,
I'd be putting myself at risk.

485
00:21:25,326 --> 00:21:26,577
0 POINTS
JIMIN CAN'T AFFORD TO HELP

486
00:21:26,660 --> 00:21:28,329
I have to survive too.

487
00:21:30,998 --> 00:21:33,000
-[♪ music fades]
-[sighs]

488
00:21:33,626 --> 00:21:36,754
[dealer]
We will begin the auction in Round 3.

489
00:21:38,672 --> 00:21:40,299
The item up for auction is...

490
00:21:40,382 --> 00:21:42,384
[♪ suspenseful music builds]

491
00:21:45,346 --> 00:21:47,807
...the collection item, "Minus."

492
00:21:47,890 --> 00:21:49,725
DISCARD ACQUIRED AUCTION ITEM
OR INHERITANCE

493
00:21:49,809 --> 00:21:51,060
What?

494
00:21:51,143 --> 00:21:52,394
[♪ suspenseful music turns tense]

495
00:21:52,478 --> 00:21:53,813
[exclaims]

496
00:21:53,896 --> 00:21:55,940
[dealer] You must discard

497
00:21:56,023 --> 00:21:59,068
either one auction item or inheritance
that you acquired.

498
00:21:59,777 --> 00:22:02,655
A collection cannot be discarded.

499
00:22:02,738 --> 00:22:04,198
If you have no items to discard,

500
00:22:04,281 --> 00:22:06,325
you must choose the next auction item

501
00:22:06,408 --> 00:22:09,745
or inheritance that is sold to you.

502
00:22:09,829 --> 00:22:10,830
[Pani Bottle exclaims]

503
00:22:11,539 --> 00:22:14,458
A collection ended up
coming out, so man...

504
00:22:14,542 --> 00:22:15,960
I absolutely can't afford to take it.

505
00:22:16,043 --> 00:22:18,587
[sighs in frustration]
Damn, this is so tough.

506
00:22:19,088 --> 00:22:21,173
I still hadn't earned any points,

507
00:22:21,257 --> 00:22:23,592
but a collection
would put me in the negatives.

508
00:22:23,676 --> 00:22:26,470
That's when I started getting worried.

509
00:22:26,554 --> 00:22:27,930
I was actually pretty happy.

510
00:22:28,013 --> 00:22:30,099
Because I had the most money then.

511
00:22:30,182 --> 00:22:32,977
So, if everyone else was losing money,
that was good for me.

512
00:22:33,060 --> 00:22:35,354
Even if I lost some,
I'd still come out ahead.

513
00:22:36,605 --> 00:22:38,482
[dealer] Ms. Jang Eunsil,
please state your bid.

514
00:22:39,817 --> 00:22:40,818
I bid 3 million.

515
00:22:40,901 --> 00:22:42,361
-I bid 5 million.
-[dealer] We have 5 million.

516
00:22:42,444 --> 00:22:43,445
Mr. Pani Bottle.

517
00:22:44,780 --> 00:22:46,365
-I bid 10 million.
-[dealer] We have 10 million.

518
00:22:50,035 --> 00:22:51,328
-I bid 11 million.
-[dealer] We have 11 million.

519
00:22:51,412 --> 00:22:52,413
Ms. Jang Eunsil?

520
00:22:53,789 --> 00:22:54,790
I'll just drop out.

521
00:22:56,292 --> 00:23:00,421
[dealer] Ms. Jang Eunsil
is the first to drop out.

522
00:23:02,590 --> 00:23:04,884
ROUND 3, AUCTION 1
MINUS POINTS

523
00:23:04,967 --> 00:23:07,928
[Ddolddol] Losing 10 points
is too much of a critical hit.

524
00:23:08,637 --> 00:23:10,973
[Junseo] This might be
where the eliminations are decided.

525
00:23:11,056 --> 00:23:13,058
[♪ music intensifies]

526
00:23:16,228 --> 00:23:18,272
[Eunsil]
I actually didn't have much money.

527
00:23:18,898 --> 00:23:21,275
[dealer] Ms. Jang Eunsil,
you must pay 41 million won.

528
00:23:21,358 --> 00:23:23,736
Sold to Ms. Jang Eunsil
for 120 million won.

529
00:23:23,819 --> 00:23:24,820
SPENT TOTAL 161 MILLION WON

530
00:23:24,904 --> 00:23:27,907
JANG EUNSIL
CURRENT CASH: 39 MILLION WON

531
00:23:29,241 --> 00:23:30,284
[Eunsil] Wait a minute.

532
00:23:31,160 --> 00:23:34,788
I counted my money
and realized I was practically broke.

533
00:23:38,417 --> 00:23:41,295
I had so little cash
that my mind went blank.

534
00:23:41,378 --> 00:23:43,213
The more I bid,

535
00:23:43,297 --> 00:23:46,759
the less cash I had,
so I became very nervous.

536
00:23:46,842 --> 00:23:48,969
I couldn't afford to gamble.

537
00:23:49,053 --> 00:23:51,055
[♪ tense music continues playing]

538
00:23:55,059 --> 00:23:56,268
This was too pricey to buy.

539
00:23:56,352 --> 00:23:58,354
EUNSIL CONSERVES LAST AMOUNT OF CASH

540
00:23:58,437 --> 00:23:59,855
AUCTION STATUS
1ST: EUNSIL, 10 POINTS

541
00:23:59,939 --> 00:24:01,106
TIED FOR 4TH: EUNSIL, 0 POINTS

542
00:24:01,190 --> 00:24:05,152
PANI BOTTLE AND JANG EUNSIL
IN DANGER OF ELIMINATION

543
00:24:05,986 --> 00:24:08,572
[Pani Bottle whispering] I might be able
to survive with just one point.

544
00:24:08,656 --> 00:24:10,574
-[Jimin] Does Eunsil have zero points?
-[Pani Bottle] Yeah.

545
00:24:10,658 --> 00:24:12,743
[♪ exhilarating music builds]

546
00:24:12,826 --> 00:24:15,829
I was worried about what I'd do
if my turn came around,

547
00:24:16,497 --> 00:24:18,916
but then Eunsil bought it.

548
00:24:18,999 --> 00:24:20,167
I was grateful.

549
00:24:20,250 --> 00:24:22,002
I thought I had a real chance now.

550
00:24:22,086 --> 00:24:23,087
THERE'S STILL A WAY OUT

551
00:24:23,170 --> 00:24:26,507
I was in last place, but suddenly,
two people tied with zero points.

552
00:24:28,884 --> 00:24:30,177
I asked Ddolddol for a favor.

553
00:24:31,387 --> 00:24:35,140
I told him I needed this next one
or I'd be stuck in the negatives forever.

554
00:24:35,224 --> 00:24:36,934
[dealer] We will move on to the next item.

555
00:24:37,017 --> 00:24:38,102
SECOND AUCTION

556
00:24:39,687 --> 00:24:42,564
The 5th Grade item, "High Heels."

557
00:24:42,648 --> 00:24:45,317
The winning bid will receive five points.

558
00:24:45,943 --> 00:24:48,487
[Pani Bottle] Okay, we're good.
I can definitely buy this.

559
00:24:49,113 --> 00:24:51,031
-I bid 2 million.
-[Junseo] I bid 4 million.

560
00:24:51,657 --> 00:24:53,367
-I bid 16 million.
-[dealer] We have 16 million.

561
00:24:53,450 --> 00:24:55,035
I'm out.

562
00:24:55,119 --> 00:24:57,246
I bid 30 million. I bid 45 million.

563
00:24:57,329 --> 00:24:58,664
I'm out.

564
00:24:59,331 --> 00:25:00,374
I am out.

565
00:25:00,457 --> 00:25:02,459
-[dealer] Mr. Kim Ddolddol.
-I'm out.

566
00:25:02,543 --> 00:25:05,671
Pani Bottle and I
had our brotherly alliance,

567
00:25:05,754 --> 00:25:08,048
so I dropped out to help him.

568
00:25:08,132 --> 00:25:12,261
[dealer] Sold to Mr. Pani Bottle
for 45 million won.

569
00:25:12,344 --> 00:25:16,432
[Pani Bottle] Five points isn't much
compared to the previous items.

570
00:25:16,515 --> 00:25:19,685
So, the others didn't really
have a reason to go for it.

571
00:25:19,768 --> 00:25:22,354
And I got it for a pretty decent deal.

572
00:25:22,938 --> 00:25:25,315
If I get one more item,
I've got this in the bag.

573
00:25:25,399 --> 00:25:26,984
[♪ music stops]

574
00:25:30,154 --> 00:25:32,156
[♪ intriguing music playing]

575
00:25:33,949 --> 00:25:34,950
[Jimin whispering] What's your score?

576
00:25:35,034 --> 00:25:36,368
-[Sanghyun] What?
-[Jimin] What's your score?

577
00:25:36,452 --> 00:25:38,037
[Sanghyun] I don't have that many points.

578
00:25:40,706 --> 00:25:42,124
[dealer speaking indistinctly]

579
00:25:43,375 --> 00:25:45,669
[Jimin] I had no points,

580
00:25:46,253 --> 00:25:49,715
and with only a few auction items left,
I knew I had to make a move.

581
00:25:49,798 --> 00:25:51,592
We will unveil the auction item.

582
00:25:52,134 --> 00:25:56,138
The 2nd Grade item, Hyeolanbirok.

583
00:25:56,221 --> 00:25:59,308
The winning bid will receive nine points.

584
00:26:00,309 --> 00:26:03,562
[Jimin] Everyone had spent
a lot of money in Round 1.

585
00:26:04,229 --> 00:26:08,150
So in that situation, I could survive
if I could get nine points.

586
00:26:08,734 --> 00:26:12,571
Even if I had to pay a lot,
I was going to get it, no matter what.

587
00:26:14,073 --> 00:26:15,365
[dealer] Mr. Pani Bottle.

588
00:26:15,449 --> 00:26:17,284
-[Pani Bottle] I bid 5 million won.
-[dealer] We have 5 million won.

589
00:26:17,367 --> 00:26:19,244
-Mr. Youn Sanghyun?
-I'm out.

590
00:26:19,328 --> 00:26:21,121
-I'm out.
-I'm out.

591
00:26:21,205 --> 00:26:22,372
[dealer] Mr. Kim Ddolddol has dropped out.

592
00:26:22,998 --> 00:26:23,999
Ms. Park Jimin.

593
00:26:24,625 --> 00:26:25,793
I bid 11 million won.

594
00:26:25,876 --> 00:26:27,836
[dealer] We have 11 million.
Mr. Pani Bottle?

595
00:26:27,920 --> 00:26:30,255
-I bid 15 million.
-[dealer] We have 15 million.

596
00:26:30,839 --> 00:26:31,924
I bid 18 million.

597
00:26:32,007 --> 00:26:33,050
[Jimin] I bid 20 million.

598
00:26:33,759 --> 00:26:34,885
[Pani Bottle] I bid 25 million.

599
00:26:34,968 --> 00:26:36,261
I'm out.

600
00:26:36,345 --> 00:26:37,346
[♪ tense music playing]

601
00:26:37,429 --> 00:26:38,931
[Jimin] People started dropping out.

602
00:26:39,014 --> 00:26:41,850
Those who had already spent
nearly 100 million won

603
00:26:41,934 --> 00:26:44,311
were probably pretty hesitant
to spend a lot now.

604
00:26:44,394 --> 00:26:46,563
It was a perfect opportunity for me.

605
00:26:46,647 --> 00:26:47,648
I bid 36 million.

606
00:26:47,731 --> 00:26:49,358
[dealer] We have 36 million.
Mr. Pani Bottle?

607
00:26:49,900 --> 00:26:52,611
[Pani Bottle] With nine points,
I could get out of last place.

608
00:26:52,694 --> 00:26:54,029
I could definitely survive.

609
00:26:54,113 --> 00:26:55,280
I bid 50 million.

610
00:26:55,364 --> 00:26:57,533
I bid 56 million.

611
00:26:57,616 --> 00:26:58,784
I bid 60 million.

612
00:26:58,867 --> 00:27:00,410
I bid 61 million.

613
00:27:00,494 --> 00:27:02,496
[♪ exhilarating music playing]

614
00:27:03,288 --> 00:27:04,706
[Pani Bottle sighing] I'm out.

615
00:27:06,250 --> 00:27:10,879
[dealer] Sold to Ms. Park Jimin
for 61 million won.

616
00:27:11,880 --> 00:27:13,340
AUCTION STATUS
1ST: JIMIN, 9 POINTS

617
00:27:13,423 --> 00:27:16,385
1ST: YOUN SANGHYUN, 118 MILLION WON

618
00:27:16,468 --> 00:27:17,886
This auction item is

619
00:27:17,970 --> 00:27:20,848
the inheritance item, "Multiply by Two."

620
00:27:20,931 --> 00:27:22,015
SCORE IS DOUBLED

621
00:27:22,099 --> 00:27:23,100
[sighing] Multiply...

622
00:27:23,183 --> 00:27:25,185
PANI BOTTLE'S SCORE IS 0
MULTIPLY BY 2 IS STILL 0

623
00:27:28,272 --> 00:27:29,565
[Jimin] I got so excited.

624
00:27:29,648 --> 00:27:33,068
I had nine points.
Double that, and it's 18.

625
00:27:33,735 --> 00:27:39,324
[exclaims] I wanted it so badly.
If I could get this one, I'd be done.

626
00:27:39,867 --> 00:27:40,868
I bid 8 million.

627
00:27:41,410 --> 00:27:42,619
[groans] I'm out.

628
00:27:42,703 --> 00:27:44,663
-I'm out.
-I'm out.

629
00:27:44,746 --> 00:27:48,584
[Jimin] It didn't seem like many people
were interested in "Multiply by Two."

630
00:27:48,667 --> 00:27:50,377
I bid 22 million. I bid 30 million.

631
00:27:50,460 --> 00:27:51,879
I'm out.

632
00:27:51,962 --> 00:27:53,380
-I bid 39 million.
-[dealer] We have 39 million.

633
00:27:53,463 --> 00:27:55,424
-Ms. Park Jimin.
-I bid 45 million.

634
00:27:55,507 --> 00:27:57,009
[dealer] We have 45 million.
Mr. Yuk Junseo?

635
00:27:57,092 --> 00:27:58,510
[♪ exhilarating music continues playing]

636
00:27:58,594 --> 00:27:59,636
I'm out.

637
00:27:59,720 --> 00:28:01,805
[dealer] Sold to Ms. Park Jimin.

638
00:28:01,889 --> 00:28:04,892
I don't think anyone
had a higher score than me.

639
00:28:04,975 --> 00:28:06,101
JIMIN IN 1ST WITH 18 POINTS

640
00:28:09,187 --> 00:28:11,273
AUCTION STATUS
1ST: PARK JIMIN, 18 POINTS

641
00:28:11,356 --> 00:28:16,153
2ND: PANI BOTTLE, 190 MILLION WON

642
00:28:16,236 --> 00:28:17,446
[♪ music fades]

643
00:28:17,529 --> 00:28:19,907
LAST AUCTION

644
00:28:19,990 --> 00:28:21,658
[♪ pensive music plays]

645
00:28:21,742 --> 00:28:23,160
[sighs heavily]

646
00:28:23,243 --> 00:28:25,954
PANI BOTTLE AND JANG EUNSIL
ARE TIED FOR LAST PLACE WITH 0 POINTS

647
00:28:26,538 --> 00:28:27,581
[dealer] This auction item is

648
00:28:27,664 --> 00:28:32,169
the 3rd Grade item, Starry Night.

649
00:28:32,252 --> 00:28:34,838
The winning bid will receive eight points.

650
00:28:34,922 --> 00:28:36,965
-[♪ pensive music turns tense]
-[exclaims]

651
00:28:37,049 --> 00:28:39,676
This auction will be a blind auction.

652
00:28:39,760 --> 00:28:43,722
Please write your bid and submit it
in the envelope we have provided.

653
00:28:43,805 --> 00:28:45,557
[sighs heavily]

654
00:28:45,641 --> 00:28:47,601
[Pani Bottle]
I really didn't want to be eliminated,

655
00:28:47,684 --> 00:28:50,228
so I started doing the math
and kept thinking.

656
00:28:50,312 --> 00:28:52,105
As long as I kept more money than Eunsil

657
00:28:52,189 --> 00:28:53,857
"EUNSIL 36 MILLION
PANI BOTTLE 109 MILLION"

658
00:28:53,941 --> 00:28:55,317
and used the rest for my bid,

659
00:28:55,400 --> 00:28:56,401
"AVAILABLE CASH: 72 MILLION"

660
00:28:56,485 --> 00:28:57,486
I'd definitely survive.

661
00:28:57,569 --> 00:28:59,571
[♪ music intensifies]

662
00:29:03,575 --> 00:29:05,953
[Sanghyun]
What happens if there's a tie in points?

663
00:29:06,036 --> 00:29:09,039
What if two people are tied
for the lowest score?

664
00:29:09,122 --> 00:29:12,709
[dealer] If two people are tied
for the lowest score,

665
00:29:13,251 --> 00:29:16,296
the player with less cash on hand
will be eliminated.

666
00:29:16,380 --> 00:29:17,923
[Sanghyun] Mmm...

667
00:29:21,093 --> 00:29:23,804
[whispering] So cash matters too.

668
00:29:26,264 --> 00:29:27,265
Geez.

669
00:29:27,975 --> 00:29:29,101
I'm so doomed.

670
00:29:29,810 --> 00:29:31,478
Seriously.

671
00:29:32,020 --> 00:29:35,399
[host] The final two eliminations
will be determined in the following order.

672
00:29:35,482 --> 00:29:36,692
GOING OVER RULES BEFORE AUCTION

673
00:29:36,775 --> 00:29:40,362
First, the player with the lowest
auction score is eliminated.

674
00:29:40,445 --> 00:29:44,074
If two or more players are tied
for the lowest auction score,

675
00:29:44,157 --> 00:29:48,203
the player with the least
amount of cash is eliminated.

676
00:29:48,286 --> 00:29:51,665
Next, the player with the least
amount of cash among the remaining players

677
00:29:51,748 --> 00:29:52,958
is eliminated.

678
00:29:53,041 --> 00:29:55,085
[♪ unsettling music playing]

679
00:29:55,168 --> 00:29:57,295
[Jimin] I'm in big trouble.

680
00:29:57,379 --> 00:30:01,341
Between Eunsil and Pani Bottle,
Eunsil has less cash, so she's eliminated.

681
00:30:01,425 --> 00:30:02,634
JANG EUNSIL ELIMINATION CONFIRMED

682
00:30:02,718 --> 00:30:04,720
I had the second-lowest amount
of cash after her,

683
00:30:04,803 --> 00:30:06,346
so I was at risk of elimination.

684
00:30:06,930 --> 00:30:09,891
The only way I could survive
was for Pani Bottle

685
00:30:09,975 --> 00:30:12,561
to spend big and win the auction.

686
00:30:14,563 --> 00:30:15,772
[Pani Bottle whispering]
Jimin, wait a second.

687
00:30:15,856 --> 00:30:17,941
[dealer speaking indistinctly]

688
00:30:18,025 --> 00:30:21,319
[Jimin] Just then, Pani Bottle kept saying

689
00:30:21,403 --> 00:30:24,114
that he absolutely had to get this item.

690
00:30:24,197 --> 00:30:25,657
Hey, this is great news.

691
00:30:26,575 --> 00:30:27,868
[mouthing] Let me get it, okay?

692
00:30:27,951 --> 00:30:28,994
[mouthing] Yeah, I know.

693
00:30:29,786 --> 00:30:33,206
I pretended to be nice
and encouraged him to buy it.

694
00:30:33,290 --> 00:30:35,292
[♪ unsettling music continues playing]

695
00:30:53,226 --> 00:30:54,227
[♪ music fades]

696
00:30:54,311 --> 00:30:55,687
[dealer] The auction is now closed.

697
00:30:55,771 --> 00:30:57,731
[♪ ominous music builds]

698
00:30:57,814 --> 00:31:02,652
We have determined the winning bidder.
The winning bid is 73 million won.

699
00:31:02,736 --> 00:31:04,696
[exclaims] Someone made that bid?

700
00:31:04,780 --> 00:31:07,240
[♪ ominous music turns tense]

701
00:31:07,657 --> 00:31:10,911
[dealer] We will reveal the final results.

702
00:31:11,495 --> 00:31:14,748
The first elimination goes to the player
with the lowest score,

703
00:31:14,831 --> 00:31:16,875
Jang Eunsil.

704
00:31:16,958 --> 00:31:19,086
JANG EUNSIL IS ELIMINATED
WITH LOWEST SCORE

705
00:31:21,379 --> 00:31:23,381
[♪ music fades]

706
00:31:23,465 --> 00:31:24,800
The second elimination...

707
00:31:24,883 --> 00:31:26,843
[♪ tense music resumes playing]

708
00:31:26,927 --> 00:31:32,140
[sighing in despair]
Please, I just want one more chance.

709
00:31:32,224 --> 00:31:35,894
I really didn't want to be eliminated.
I wanted to stay so badly

710
00:31:35,977 --> 00:31:38,438
that I couldn't even think straight.

711
00:31:39,106 --> 00:31:41,900
[dealer] The second elimination
goes to the player

712
00:31:41,983 --> 00:31:43,068
with the least amount of cash...

713
00:31:43,151 --> 00:31:45,153
[♪ music intensifies]

714
00:31:48,615 --> 00:31:50,075
...Pani Bottle.

715
00:31:50,158 --> 00:31:52,327
PANI BOTTLE, ELIMINATED
WITH LEAST AMOUNT OF CASH

716
00:31:52,410 --> 00:31:54,037
-[sighing] I messed up the math.
-[♪ music stops]

717
00:31:54,621 --> 00:31:58,583
PARK JIMIN SURVIVES IN 4TH PLACE
FINAL CASH AMOUNT: 46 MILLION WON

718
00:31:58,667 --> 00:32:00,669
[♪ somber music playing]

719
00:32:00,752 --> 00:32:03,255
[sighs heavily] I'm such a fucking idiot.

720
00:32:04,089 --> 00:32:08,969
I felt this cold, sinking feeling
spread through my chest then.

721
00:32:09,636 --> 00:32:10,637
[groans]

722
00:32:11,513 --> 00:32:14,224
I'd basically won,
but I threw it away with my own mistake.

723
00:32:15,016 --> 00:32:18,395
Looking back, I was so obsessed
that I wasn't thinking straight.

724
00:32:19,646 --> 00:32:21,356
Eunsil was confirmed to be eliminated.

725
00:32:21,439 --> 00:32:25,193
Then, the one with the least
amount of cash would be eliminated.

726
00:32:25,277 --> 00:32:26,945
I didn't even have to buy that item.

727
00:32:27,487 --> 00:32:29,156
But I got so busy counting money.

728
00:32:29,239 --> 00:32:31,032
I didn't even need to spend at all,

729
00:32:31,116 --> 00:32:32,701
but I put in a bid of 73 million won.

730
00:32:32,784 --> 00:32:34,327
PANI BOTTLE
73 MILLION

731
00:32:36,204 --> 00:32:39,416
[inhales sharply] Wait, was that right?
I can't do the math.

732
00:32:42,252 --> 00:32:43,587
Wait a second. [groans]

733
00:32:43,670 --> 00:32:45,422
REALIZED CALCULATION MISTAKE TOO LATE

734
00:32:45,505 --> 00:32:46,715
I think I messed up the math.

735
00:32:46,798 --> 00:32:48,633
Up until the results
were announced, I hoped,

736
00:32:48,717 --> 00:32:51,344
"Maybe I've already won,
and I'm probably just mistaken."

737
00:32:51,428 --> 00:32:54,055
And when my name was called
as the second elimination,

738
00:32:54,139 --> 00:32:55,765
my heart just sank.

739
00:32:56,558 --> 00:32:58,268
-I didn't even feel sad...
-I had it wrong.

740
00:32:58,351 --> 00:32:59,436
...or angry or anything.

741
00:32:59,519 --> 00:33:00,604
I calculated it wrong.

742
00:33:00,687 --> 00:33:01,688
I just thought,

743
00:33:02,314 --> 00:33:05,442
"Maybe I'm just not good enough.
This is the extent of my abilities."

744
00:33:05,525 --> 00:33:06,902
I couldn't help but think that.

745
00:33:06,985 --> 00:33:09,154
FINAL RESULTS
6TH: JANG EUNSIL, 0 POINTS

746
00:33:09,237 --> 00:33:10,697
5TH: PANI BOTTLE, 36 MILLION WON

747
00:33:10,780 --> 00:33:13,867
JANG EUNSIL, PANI BOTTLE ELIMINATED

748
00:33:14,659 --> 00:33:16,578
[dealer]
Ms. Jang Eunsil and Mr. Pani Bottle,

749
00:33:16,661 --> 00:33:18,997
please exit the area immediately.

750
00:33:19,497 --> 00:33:21,499
[♪ somber music turns tense]

751
00:33:24,419 --> 00:33:28,757
Eliminated players will not be able
to return to Deadly Tag.

752
00:33:28,840 --> 00:33:30,008
[♪ music fades]

753
00:33:30,091 --> 00:33:33,386
It's my own fault.
I made a miscalculation.

754
00:33:33,470 --> 00:33:36,765
In the end, with one win and four losses,

755
00:33:37,807 --> 00:33:39,059
that was the end of my run.

756
00:33:39,142 --> 00:33:40,143
Fuck.

757
00:33:41,186 --> 00:33:44,231
I prepared a lot
for this reality survival show

758
00:33:44,314 --> 00:33:45,732
and really wanted to do well.

759
00:33:45,815 --> 00:33:50,779
But I always seemed to make big mistakes
at crucial moments.

760
00:33:50,862 --> 00:33:51,905
I'm out.

761
00:33:51,988 --> 00:33:54,407
I guess I felt too much pressure.

762
00:33:54,491 --> 00:33:56,868
[inhales sharply]
So, I'm very disappointed in myself.

763
00:33:57,702 --> 00:34:00,914
I just wanted to survive
and keep having fun.

764
00:34:00,997 --> 00:34:02,999
[♪ lilting music playing]

765
00:34:04,834 --> 00:34:05,877
Do it now!

766
00:34:07,712 --> 00:34:09,047
Put it there after three minutes.

767
00:34:09,130 --> 00:34:10,632
-I won.
-[Ddolddol] Nice.

768
00:34:10,715 --> 00:34:11,883
-You played your 5?
-[Pani Bottle] Yes.

769
00:34:11,967 --> 00:34:13,343
-[Ddolddol] No way.
-Then, he must have a 2.

770
00:34:13,426 --> 00:34:14,427
Yeah, a 2.

771
00:34:15,470 --> 00:34:17,973
I experienced
all kinds of emotions in here.

772
00:34:18,056 --> 00:34:19,432
I said I wanted to talk.

773
00:34:19,516 --> 00:34:20,517
[Jimin] If I hadn't been on this team...

774
00:34:20,600 --> 00:34:21,935
-[sobs]
-[Pani Bottle sniffles]

775
00:34:22,018 --> 00:34:24,020
PANI BOTTLE GAVE HIS ALL IN EVERY MOMENT

776
00:34:25,146 --> 00:34:26,398
[inhales sharply]

777
00:34:26,481 --> 00:34:29,859
And I'm tearing up again.
Let's give it a rest now.

778
00:34:32,237 --> 00:34:35,407
[Sanghyun] You did great.
It was a bit of a shame at the end.

779
00:34:36,157 --> 00:34:37,158
Good job.

780
00:34:38,410 --> 00:34:40,370
It felt bittersweet.

781
00:34:40,912 --> 00:34:46,334
I was eliminated because I came up short,
so I don't have many regrets.

782
00:34:46,918 --> 00:34:50,964
JANG EUNSIL GAVE IT EVERYTHING SHE HAD

783
00:34:51,047 --> 00:34:52,382
-[Eunsil] Tag! I got you first.
-[Horseking] No, I did.

784
00:34:52,465 --> 00:34:53,717
-[Eunsil] It was a bang-bang play.
-[Horseking] Exactly!

785
00:34:54,259 --> 00:34:57,262
[Eunsil] I worked as a part of teams too.

786
00:34:57,846 --> 00:34:59,848
[♪ lilting music continues playing]

787
00:35:01,308 --> 00:35:04,102
We shared a lot of emotions
while playing the game together,

788
00:35:04,185 --> 00:35:06,563
and I think I learned a lot.

789
00:35:07,063 --> 00:35:10,942
[Jimin] What am I supposed to do now?

790
00:35:12,485 --> 00:35:13,528
Bye.

791
00:35:16,323 --> 00:35:17,699
I felt bad.

792
00:35:19,701 --> 00:35:24,789
EUNSIL LEFT A NOTE FOR JIMIN

793
00:35:25,373 --> 00:35:26,666
-[exclaims]
-[♪ melancholic music playing]

794
00:35:26,750 --> 00:35:29,294
JIMIN, I'LL HEAD OUT FIRST
I HAD SO MUCH FUN WITH YOU HERE

795
00:35:29,377 --> 00:35:30,420
"This lousy..."

796
00:35:30,503 --> 00:35:32,839
I'LL CHERISH THIS MEMORY
SEE YOU WHEN DEADLY TAG ENDS

797
00:35:33,465 --> 00:35:36,801
I'm getting really choked up.

798
00:35:41,014 --> 00:35:42,015
[sniffles]

799
00:35:42,766 --> 00:35:43,808
[murmurs] Hold on...

800
00:35:47,020 --> 00:35:50,565
Eunsil and I relied on each other a lot.

801
00:35:52,400 --> 00:35:54,194
I was so grateful for her.

802
00:35:54,277 --> 00:35:58,657
I'll make sure to win,

803
00:35:58,740 --> 00:36:01,618
and I'll treat you to a nice meal.

804
00:36:01,701 --> 00:36:03,620
Let's definitely meet up on the outside.
[sniffles]

805
00:36:03,703 --> 00:36:04,704
[♪ music fades]

806
00:36:04,788 --> 00:36:09,084
[Eunsil] I really hope
Jimin makes it all the way to the end

807
00:36:09,167 --> 00:36:10,794
and first and foremost catches the Seeker.

808
00:36:10,877 --> 00:36:15,799
The Seeker makes me so mad.
Who on earth is it? Are they nuts?

809
00:36:15,882 --> 00:36:17,592
What on earth are you doing?

810
00:36:17,676 --> 00:36:18,677
[♪ quirky music plays]

811
00:36:18,760 --> 00:36:22,681
THE SEEKER WAS ACTUALLY CLOSER
THAN SHE REALIZED

812
00:36:23,306 --> 00:36:25,350
[host] The Death Match has ended.

813
00:36:25,433 --> 00:36:27,435
[♪ ominous music playing]

814
00:36:31,981 --> 00:36:33,525
[Dail] Wait, are you back, Junseo?

815
00:36:33,608 --> 00:36:34,651
[Junseo] Yeah.

816
00:36:35,610 --> 00:36:37,112
[Dail] Junseo, you're back?

817
00:36:37,612 --> 00:36:38,697
[Ddolddol] We're back.

818
00:36:38,780 --> 00:36:40,115
Pani Bottle and...

819
00:36:40,198 --> 00:36:41,324
[Dail] Yeah.

820
00:36:41,408 --> 00:36:42,659
Wait, Ddolddol is here too?

821
00:36:42,742 --> 00:36:44,411
[Ddolddol] And Eunsil got eliminated.

822
00:36:44,494 --> 00:36:46,329
[Dail] What a relief.

823
00:36:47,038 --> 00:36:48,289
Four people came back.

824
00:36:48,373 --> 00:36:50,917
[Ddolddol] Park Jimin, Yuk Junseo, me,

825
00:36:51,000 --> 00:36:52,502
and Sanghyun.

826
00:36:52,585 --> 00:36:54,379
[Dail] Jimin is hanging on pretty well.

827
00:36:58,425 --> 00:37:00,385
[Joonsu]
Jimin's lasting longer than I expected.

828
00:37:02,887 --> 00:37:07,684
How is she still managing to survive?
She's not someone to underestimate.

829
00:37:08,768 --> 00:37:09,769
[Dail] Horseking.

830
00:37:09,853 --> 00:37:10,937
[Horseking] Yeah?

831
00:37:11,020 --> 00:37:12,272
[Dail] Who is the Seeker?

832
00:37:13,314 --> 00:37:16,359
Shouldn't we just pick the person
we suspect now?

833
00:37:17,026 --> 00:37:18,695
[Dail] I really have no idea.

834
00:37:18,778 --> 00:37:21,489
Let's just see if the Seeker
completed their mission.

835
00:37:21,573 --> 00:37:22,574
[Dail] Yeah.

836
00:37:22,657 --> 00:37:23,950
Then, we'll talk about it.

837
00:37:25,785 --> 00:37:28,413
[Jimin] It feels like
we'll do the Seeker Vote today.

838
00:37:28,496 --> 00:37:30,498
If they all vote for me, I'm out.

839
00:37:32,459 --> 00:37:33,918
[mic feedback]

840
00:37:34,002 --> 00:37:36,713
[host] Everyone,
please gather in the Main Hall.

841
00:37:37,839 --> 00:37:39,591
[Horseking] Sanghyun, you're back.

842
00:37:39,674 --> 00:37:41,676
[♪ ominous music playing]

843
00:37:47,223 --> 00:37:52,479
I was so nervous.
My hands and feet were drenched in sweat.

844
00:37:52,562 --> 00:37:54,439
My heart was beating out of my chest.

845
00:37:55,940 --> 00:37:57,692
[mic feedback]

846
00:38:00,153 --> 00:38:02,906
[host] We will now begin the Seeker Vote.

847
00:38:04,407 --> 00:38:07,202
Before the Seeker Vote,
we have an announcement.

848
00:38:08,244 --> 00:38:11,414
In the Main Match, "Kingmaker,"

849
00:38:13,875 --> 00:38:15,168
the Seeker...

850
00:38:18,213 --> 00:38:19,589
completed their mission.

851
00:38:19,672 --> 00:38:21,591
[♪ music stops]

852
00:38:23,218 --> 00:38:24,219
[Joonsu] What happened?

853
00:38:24,302 --> 00:38:28,932
[host] By completing their mission,
the Seeker will gain a special benefit.

854
00:38:30,600 --> 00:38:34,229
[exclaims] The Seeker completed
their mission amid that chaos?

855
00:38:34,312 --> 00:38:35,355
That's impressive.

856
00:38:35,438 --> 00:38:38,107
-[exclaims] I'm getting so mad.
-[Horseking] What did they do?

857
00:38:38,191 --> 00:38:41,152
[Dail] The Seeker is so good at this game.

858
00:38:41,277 --> 00:38:42,445
It's really stressing me out.

859
00:38:42,529 --> 00:38:46,366
What mission did they complete yesterday?
Was there even a mission?

860
00:38:46,449 --> 00:38:48,743
Right? When did they even do that?

861
00:38:48,827 --> 00:38:51,579
[Jimin] Of course, I was proud.
Come on, it's me.

862
00:38:53,706 --> 00:38:56,501
"KINGMAKER" SEEKER MISSION
RECEIVED IN ADVANCE

863
00:38:56,584 --> 00:38:59,921
The mission was to "compete
against the opposing team three times."

864
00:39:00,630 --> 00:39:05,343
Once I had the Joker, I knew getting
those three matchups wouldn't be too hard.

865
00:39:06,302 --> 00:39:09,180
1ST WITH HORSEKING

866
00:39:10,139 --> 00:39:12,141
2ND AND 3RD WITH JOONSU

867
00:39:12,225 --> 00:39:14,102
-[Joonsu exclaims]
-[Jimin] I got you! Tag!

868
00:39:14,185 --> 00:39:16,062
[♪ electronic music plays]

869
00:39:16,646 --> 00:39:18,481
THREE MATCHUPS EASILY COMPLETED

870
00:39:19,524 --> 00:39:20,567
[ZZONE] I have no idea.

871
00:39:21,359 --> 00:39:25,321
[host] Please complete the Seeker Vote
within the next hour.

872
00:39:25,405 --> 00:39:27,407
[♪ music fades]

873
00:39:30,326 --> 00:39:33,079
Was there even time
to do a mission yesterday?

874
00:39:33,162 --> 00:39:34,372
-[Dail] Exactly.
-[ZZONE] Right?

875
00:39:34,956 --> 00:39:37,166
But tagging someone
or being tagged by someone

876
00:39:37,250 --> 00:39:38,251
-is doable.
-[Jaegyun] You think so?

877
00:39:38,334 --> 00:39:39,669
I was sure the Seeker had failed.

878
00:39:39,752 --> 00:39:41,671
[Ddolddol]
Did they break a symbol on purpose?

879
00:39:41,754 --> 00:39:43,590
They broke what they're supposed to bring.

880
00:39:43,673 --> 00:39:47,427
The only ones who collected symbols
were me and Pani Bottle on our team.

881
00:39:47,510 --> 00:39:50,263
[Jimin] But that sabotages our team.

882
00:39:50,805 --> 00:39:52,807
That could've been the Seeker's mission.

883
00:39:52,891 --> 00:39:54,893
[Jimin] But that doesn't make sense.

884
00:39:54,976 --> 00:39:58,354
The Seeker was given a mission
to lose then?

885
00:39:58,438 --> 00:40:00,523
-It can't be breaking symbols.
-[Jimin] If that's the case,

886
00:40:00,607 --> 00:40:05,236
the Seeker needs their team to lose,
but that would eliminated them too.

887
00:40:05,320 --> 00:40:07,989
So you're saying their mission
wasn't about hurting the team?

888
00:40:08,072 --> 00:40:09,073
[Sanghyun] That's right.

889
00:40:09,157 --> 00:40:12,619
[Jimin] This time, my strategy
was to convince them that the Seeker

890
00:40:12,702 --> 00:40:14,704
could be on the winning team too.

891
00:40:14,787 --> 00:40:16,456
[♪ intriguing music playing]

892
00:40:16,539 --> 00:40:21,002
[groans] I still can't figure out
who the Seeker is.

893
00:40:21,711 --> 00:40:24,714
I was so frustrated
by how things played out.

894
00:40:25,798 --> 00:40:26,799
It was frustrating.

895
00:40:27,717 --> 00:40:30,678
I'm sure each team
stuck to the plans they came up with.

896
00:40:30,762 --> 00:40:31,763
-[Ddolddol] Yeah.
-[Jaegyun] Right.

897
00:40:31,846 --> 00:40:34,182
Was there anyone
who didn't follow those plans?

898
00:40:34,265 --> 00:40:38,645
No one on our team went off script.
Everyone followed it perfectly.

899
00:40:38,728 --> 00:40:40,605
-There's only one then.
-[Jaegyun] Only one.

900
00:40:40,688 --> 00:40:42,732
-[Dail giggles]
-That was a big surprise.

901
00:40:43,650 --> 00:40:45,568
At this point,
you need to go after Junseo.

902
00:40:45,652 --> 00:40:46,694
YESTERDAY DURING "KINGMAKER"

903
00:40:46,778 --> 00:40:49,864
You have an 8.
It's definitely higher than Junseo's card.

904
00:40:49,948 --> 00:40:51,950
[♪ ominous music playing]

905
00:40:55,036 --> 00:40:58,039
[ZZONE] Tag, tag!

906
00:40:58,831 --> 00:41:00,041
[Dail] I was supposed to tag him.

907
00:41:00,124 --> 00:41:01,125
What?

908
00:41:01,209 --> 00:41:02,877
ZZONE WENT AGAINST PLANS

909
00:41:03,920 --> 00:41:08,049
The only explanation that made sense to me
was that she was the Seeker.

910
00:41:08,132 --> 00:41:12,512
Considering how it played out,
it was natural to suspect me.

911
00:41:12,595 --> 00:41:16,307
After that, I did my best to hide
and bring in the symbols.

912
00:41:16,391 --> 00:41:19,519
[Sanghyun]
I've always been suspicious of Jimin,

913
00:41:19,602 --> 00:41:21,604
and I was also suspicious of ZZONE.

914
00:41:22,188 --> 00:41:23,189
-ZZONE...
-[Pani Bottle] Hold on.

915
00:41:23,272 --> 00:41:24,273
I think she's the Seeker.

916
00:41:24,357 --> 00:41:25,358
LAST NIGHT
BEFORE DEATH MATCH

917
00:41:25,441 --> 00:41:26,609
[Sanghyun] ZZONE could be the Seeker.

918
00:41:26,693 --> 00:41:27,986
[Pani Bottle]
Even her team is suspicious of her.

919
00:41:28,069 --> 00:41:29,570
Her team today suspects her too.

920
00:41:29,654 --> 00:41:30,905
-[Sanghyun] Really?
-[Jimin] Once this is over,

921
00:41:30,989 --> 00:41:32,407
I'm voting for ZZONE as the Seeker.

922
00:41:33,282 --> 00:41:37,662
I'd been pushing ZZONE as the Seeker
even before the Death Match.

923
00:41:37,745 --> 00:41:41,165
And fortunately,
everyone was starting to suspect her.

924
00:41:41,749 --> 00:41:43,584
[indistinct chatter]

925
00:41:44,377 --> 00:41:45,378
Joonsu.

926
00:41:46,671 --> 00:41:47,672
[♪ intriguing music playing]

927
00:41:47,755 --> 00:41:51,634
THE TWO SUDDENLY GO OFF TO TALK PRIVATELY

928
00:41:52,218 --> 00:41:53,970
[Horseking]
What on earth did they complete?

929
00:41:56,347 --> 00:41:58,683
[Jimin] Sanghyun kept pulling people aside
one by one.

930
00:41:59,475 --> 00:42:02,854
[Sanghyun] At first, in the Main Match,
"Time Between Dogs and Wolves,"

931
00:42:02,937 --> 00:42:05,773
-you were on the same team with ZZONE.
-[Joonsu] Right.

932
00:42:05,857 --> 00:42:07,650
Your plan was to get tagged.

933
00:42:08,359 --> 00:42:09,360
-[Joonsu] That's right.
-Right?

934
00:42:09,444 --> 00:42:10,486
Who came up with that plan?

935
00:42:10,570 --> 00:42:11,612
-[Joonsu] ZZONE.
-Exactly.

936
00:42:13,656 --> 00:42:15,116
I'm so suspicious of her.

937
00:42:15,783 --> 00:42:19,454
ZZONE has won so many games.

938
00:42:19,537 --> 00:42:21,080
Yesterday was extremely suspicious.

939
00:42:22,290 --> 00:42:25,626
JIMIN IS ANXIOUS
ABOUT THE SITUATION UPSTAIRS

940
00:42:26,210 --> 00:42:29,338
[Jimin]
Did Joonsu take Sanghyun over there?

941
00:42:30,798 --> 00:42:34,886
I was so anxious since I had no idea
what they were talking about.

942
00:42:34,969 --> 00:42:37,263
Sanghyun can be quite convincing.

943
00:42:37,346 --> 00:42:39,140
People seem to listen to him.

944
00:42:40,475 --> 00:42:41,642
Sanghyun is here.

945
00:42:41,726 --> 00:42:42,977
[Horseking] Did you go discuss something?

946
00:42:43,061 --> 00:42:44,062
[Sanghyun] Yes, we talked.

947
00:42:45,271 --> 00:42:47,231
[Jimin] With Sanghyun...

948
00:42:47,315 --> 00:42:48,399
-[Horseking] What? Okay.
-[Jimin] Let's talk.

949
00:42:48,483 --> 00:42:50,151
Could we talk for a moment?

950
00:42:50,902 --> 00:42:53,488
I figured I had to convince Sanghyun.

951
00:42:54,280 --> 00:42:55,907
What's on your mind?

952
00:42:57,533 --> 00:43:01,120
Mmm... Honestly,
I'm suspicious of you and ZZONE.

953
00:43:01,788 --> 00:43:02,789
-[Horseking] It's one of the two?
-[Sanghyun] Yes.

954
00:43:02,872 --> 00:43:04,040
I don't know what happened

955
00:43:04,123 --> 00:43:05,958
-in the Main Match yesterday.
-[Jimin] Yeah.

956
00:43:06,042 --> 00:43:08,377
[chuckling] So I just looked
at their reactions earlier.

957
00:43:08,461 --> 00:43:10,129
But why do you suspect me?

958
00:43:10,213 --> 00:43:11,214
-[Sanghyun] You?
-[Jimin] Yeah.

959
00:43:11,297 --> 00:43:14,550
Because you got tagged a lot
during "Time Between Dogs and Wolves."

960
00:43:14,634 --> 00:43:16,427
I'm not really certain though.

961
00:43:16,511 --> 00:43:21,933
My thinking is the Seeker
could've been eliminated yesterday too.

962
00:43:22,016 --> 00:43:23,434
Yeah, so tagging would be possible.

963
00:43:23,518 --> 00:43:25,520
-That would be...
-Then, who did the tagging?

964
00:43:25,603 --> 00:43:26,604
Did ZZONE tag anyone?

965
00:43:26,687 --> 00:43:27,730
CHANGES SUBJECT TO ZZONE

966
00:43:27,814 --> 00:43:30,024
-Was it a lot?
-One person.

967
00:43:30,108 --> 00:43:31,734
-Was that Junseo?
-[Horseking] Junseo. Yeah.

968
00:43:31,818 --> 00:43:33,319
[Sanghyun] That wasn't part of the plan?

969
00:43:33,402 --> 00:43:35,071
It wasn't part of the plan.

970
00:43:35,154 --> 00:43:37,657
-[Sanghyun] So, the mission...
-[Jimin] What does Joonsu think?

971
00:43:37,740 --> 00:43:41,494
I think he believes it's ZZONE.

972
00:43:42,120 --> 00:43:44,122
-[Jimin] Why?
-[Sanghyun] She looks so flustered.

973
00:43:44,205 --> 00:43:46,332
[♪ intriguing music continues playing]

974
00:43:46,415 --> 00:43:48,334
[Horseking] They say
the Seeker is one of the women.

975
00:43:49,794 --> 00:43:51,462
[Sanghyun] I hope so.

976
00:43:52,630 --> 00:43:55,424
[Horseking] Without knowing
what the Seeker mission was,

977
00:43:55,508 --> 00:43:58,845
it was hard to just pick someone.

978
00:44:01,347 --> 00:44:04,392
Hearing so many different opinions
made me really confused.

979
00:44:05,393 --> 00:44:07,019
After thinking on my own for a while,

980
00:44:07,103 --> 00:44:09,230
I wondered what I would've done
as the Seeker.

981
00:44:09,313 --> 00:44:11,315
[indistinct conversation]

982
00:44:14,277 --> 00:44:16,070
I honestly think it's Jimin.

983
00:44:16,154 --> 00:44:18,156
[♪ upbeat music playing]

984
00:44:19,907 --> 00:44:22,660
ZZONE has been voting Jimin since Round 1.

985
00:44:22,743 --> 00:44:27,874
If I were the Seeker, suspecting someone
would actually make me look suspicious.

986
00:44:27,957 --> 00:44:31,669
But Jimin has never clearly said
she was suspicious of someone.

987
00:44:32,253 --> 00:44:33,462
That's true.

988
00:44:34,088 --> 00:44:35,923
I thought it'd be
either Ddolddol or Joonsu.

989
00:44:36,007 --> 00:44:37,008
THE FIRST SEEKER VOTE

990
00:44:37,091 --> 00:44:38,259
I agree with voting out Ddolddol.

991
00:44:38,342 --> 00:44:39,343
EVERYONE SUSPECTED DDOLDDOL

992
00:44:39,427 --> 00:44:40,845
Either Ddolddol or Sanghyun.

993
00:44:40,928 --> 00:44:42,138
Okay. Then...

994
00:44:42,221 --> 00:44:43,472
-It should be him.
-[Sanghyun] Ddolddol?

995
00:44:43,556 --> 00:44:44,932
[Jieun] Is it Sanghyun?

996
00:44:46,434 --> 00:44:48,311
[Jimin] I heard from Jaegyun

997
00:44:48,978 --> 00:44:49,979
that after Ddolddol was sent off

998
00:44:50,062 --> 00:44:51,939
"SUSPICION POINT
HID BEHIND OTHERS' OPINIONS"

999
00:44:52,023 --> 00:44:53,733
he was convinced it was Sanghyun.

1000
00:44:53,816 --> 00:44:56,944
Honestly, I just want to go
with the majority.

1001
00:44:57,028 --> 00:44:58,863
So I want to hear what everyone thinks.

1002
00:44:58,946 --> 00:45:00,865
SUSPICION POINT
GOING WITH THE MAJORITY

1003
00:45:01,407 --> 00:45:02,909
She'd go, "I'll go with your opinion."

1004
00:45:02,992 --> 00:45:04,285
-That kind of stuff.
-[Sanghyun] Right.

1005
00:45:04,368 --> 00:45:06,120
-[Ddolddol] Right.
-[Horseking] But if you do that,

1006
00:45:06,746 --> 00:45:09,832
it'd make us less likely to suspect you.

1007
00:45:09,916 --> 00:45:13,002
Jimin never really seemed
to offer her own distinct opinion,

1008
00:45:13,085 --> 00:45:15,755
and she'd never target or suspect anyone.

1009
00:45:16,923 --> 00:45:20,343
I just have a feeling Jimin's the culprit.

1010
00:45:20,426 --> 00:45:21,594
I think she's the Seeker.

1011
00:45:21,677 --> 00:45:23,387
Then, let me ask you something.

1012
00:45:23,471 --> 00:45:24,847
I was going to vote for ZZONE

1013
00:45:24,931 --> 00:45:26,974
-due to what happened yesterday.
-[Horseking] Okay.

1014
00:45:27,058 --> 00:45:29,352
I heard from everyone
that she acted so weird.

1015
00:45:29,435 --> 00:45:32,230
Then, do you think
what she did was understandable?

1016
00:45:32,313 --> 00:45:35,066
To be honest, I don't understand it.
It doesn't add up.

1017
00:45:35,149 --> 00:45:37,068
[Dail] I didn't understand her actions
on two occasions.

1018
00:45:37,151 --> 00:45:41,239
I didn't understand it,
but when you're in that chaos,

1019
00:45:41,822 --> 00:45:43,616
you can just freak out. That's why...

1020
00:45:43,699 --> 00:45:46,035
I don't think she was freaking out.

1021
00:45:46,118 --> 00:45:48,996
She was just... She tagged me on her own.

1022
00:45:49,080 --> 00:45:50,498
How can that be freaking out?

1023
00:45:50,581 --> 00:45:51,707
She wasn't even in any danger.

1024
00:45:51,791 --> 00:45:52,959
I didn't see that.

1025
00:45:53,042 --> 00:45:55,127
[Dail] Junseo was running
straight toward me.

1026
00:45:55,211 --> 00:45:57,713
-[Sanghyun sighs]
-[Dail] I was right in front of him.

1027
00:45:58,130 --> 00:46:00,883
As everyone was talking,
I just started getting more confused.

1028
00:46:00,967 --> 00:46:04,220
Most of our suspicions
come from those not playing the game well.

1029
00:46:04,303 --> 00:46:07,390
Honestly, he had a clear suspect,
and that turned out to be wrong.

1030
00:46:07,473 --> 00:46:10,309
We were all wrong, but we all have
someone we suspect. Why?

1031
00:46:10,393 --> 00:46:11,894
Because we're not the Seeker.

1032
00:46:12,561 --> 00:46:18,234
But Jimin has never once clearly said
she was suspicious of anyone so far.

1033
00:46:18,317 --> 00:46:21,570
I think that may be a defense mechanism
she's using as the Seeker.

1034
00:46:21,654 --> 00:46:24,782
But that's something you might do
if you try to make people think twice.

1035
00:46:24,865 --> 00:46:29,120
I think she can think
beyond that kind of strategy.

1036
00:46:29,203 --> 00:46:32,623
[Horseking]
Junseo kept challenging what I was saying.

1037
00:46:32,707 --> 00:46:36,961
I was really frustrated and annoyed.

1038
00:46:38,045 --> 00:46:39,297
[Ddolddol] We have no idea.

1039
00:46:40,131 --> 00:46:42,133
[♪ music fades]

1040
00:46:42,216 --> 00:46:45,428
[ZZONE humming]

1041
00:46:45,511 --> 00:46:46,929
They're...

1042
00:46:47,680 --> 00:46:48,681
[sighs]

1043
00:46:49,307 --> 00:46:50,808
[Jimin groans] Everyone went off to vote,

1044
00:46:50,891 --> 00:46:52,852
and I had no idea
what they'd do this time.

1045
00:46:52,935 --> 00:46:54,937
[♪ uneasy music plays]

1046
00:46:56,105 --> 00:46:59,734
I was just praying it was ZZONE.

1047
00:47:00,359 --> 00:47:03,654
[dealer] Mr. Horseking, please vote
for who you think is the Seeker.

1048
00:47:03,738 --> 00:47:05,114
[♪ mysterious music playing]

1049
00:47:05,197 --> 00:47:07,450
[Horseking] I stuck with my opinion
and voted for Jimin.

1050
00:47:07,533 --> 00:47:08,826
SEEKER VOTE
PARK JIMIN

1051
00:47:09,618 --> 00:47:10,828
Ms. Park Jimin,

1052
00:47:10,911 --> 00:47:14,040
since you successfully cleared
the Seeker mission in the Main Match,

1053
00:47:14,123 --> 00:47:16,083
you receive two Seeker voting tickets.

1054
00:47:19,253 --> 00:47:22,590
SEEKER VOTE
ZZONE

1055
00:47:25,134 --> 00:47:27,720
SEEKER VOTE
ZZONE

1056
00:47:29,680 --> 00:47:34,101
I was so angered by ZZONE's trolling.
[chuckles softly]

1057
00:47:34,185 --> 00:47:36,312
It was weird.
The whole thing just felt off.

1058
00:47:36,896 --> 00:47:39,440
[ZZONE] I had a lot of fun
playing with you.

1059
00:47:39,523 --> 00:47:41,734
But I'm sorry,
you're definitely the Seeker.

1060
00:47:41,817 --> 00:47:42,943
SEEKER VOTE
PARK JIMIN

1061
00:47:43,027 --> 00:47:44,111
Bye, Jimin.

1062
00:47:44,195 --> 00:47:46,280
[♪ music fades]

1063
00:47:46,364 --> 00:47:49,825
[Joonsu] Will it be ZZONE or Jimin? Hello.

1064
00:47:50,451 --> 00:47:51,702
No doubt.

1065
00:47:51,786 --> 00:47:53,037
[♪ upbeat music playing]

1066
00:47:53,120 --> 00:47:55,247
[Junseo] I haven't changed my mind
about the Seeker.

1067
00:47:56,624 --> 00:47:58,709
[Sanghyun] I'm going to stand by
my convictions and vote.

1068
00:48:02,838 --> 00:48:06,217
VOTING HAS ENDED

1069
00:48:06,300 --> 00:48:08,386
[host] Please gather in the Main Hall.

1070
00:48:08,469 --> 00:48:09,470
[♪ music stops]

1071
00:48:09,553 --> 00:48:11,097
[mic feedback]

1072
00:48:12,890 --> 00:48:15,267
We will reveal the results
of the Seeker Vote.

1073
00:48:15,351 --> 00:48:17,353
-[♪ intriguing music playing]
-[exclaims]

1074
00:48:17,812 --> 00:48:21,732
The player
who received the most votes is...

1075
00:48:22,483 --> 00:48:25,569
[Jimin] I'm almost there.
Let me stay a little longer.

1076
00:48:26,737 --> 00:48:27,988
[host] ...Park Jimin.

1077
00:48:28,072 --> 00:48:30,491
ZZONE: 3 VOTES
JIMIN: 7 VOTES

1078
00:48:31,325 --> 00:48:34,620
[Jimin] The moment I heard my name,
I thought, "I'm screwed."

1079
00:48:34,703 --> 00:48:36,705
[host] Based on the Seeker Vote results,

1080
00:48:36,789 --> 00:48:39,583
your attempt to catch the Seeker

1081
00:48:39,667 --> 00:48:40,709
was successful.

1082
00:48:40,793 --> 00:48:42,878
-[all cheering]
-[♪ intriguing music turns upbeat]

1083
00:48:42,962 --> 00:48:47,550
[yelling] Jimin! I told you!
It was Park Jimin!

1084
00:48:48,134 --> 00:48:50,970
[Jimin] How did they know?
[inhales sharply]

1085
00:48:51,053 --> 00:48:55,850
I thought, "I had them all fooled
the whole time though."

1086
00:48:55,933 --> 00:48:57,560
It was such a shame to be voted out.

1087
00:48:59,186 --> 00:49:01,439
Will it be ZZONE or Jimin?

1088
00:49:02,314 --> 00:49:04,775
[Joonsu] That is the question.

1089
00:49:06,610 --> 00:49:08,112
SEEKER VOTE
PARK JIMIN

1090
00:49:08,195 --> 00:49:10,364
I was definitely going to vote for Jimin.

1091
00:49:10,448 --> 00:49:12,533
[Jaegyun] I was going to vote for Jimin.

1092
00:49:13,909 --> 00:49:16,245
[Junseo] I voted for Park Jimin.

1093
00:49:18,164 --> 00:49:19,498
[Sanghyun] I voted for Jimin.

1094
00:49:19,582 --> 00:49:20,583
SEEKER VOTE
PARK JIMIN

1095
00:49:20,666 --> 00:49:22,918
I couldn't make up my mind
right up to the end.

1096
00:49:23,002 --> 00:49:26,797
But then, something bothered me
when we were all talking.

1097
00:49:27,339 --> 00:49:28,632
-There was a time...
-[ZZONE] Yes?

1098
00:49:28,716 --> 00:49:30,885
...when Jimin was a Hunter.

1099
00:49:30,968 --> 00:49:32,636
Remember how crazy it got?

1100
00:49:32,720 --> 00:49:33,888
"Someone tagged Jimin."
"Someone tagged Jimin."

1101
00:49:33,971 --> 00:49:35,473
JUNSEO TAGGED JIMIN
JOONSU TAGGED JIMIN

1102
00:49:35,556 --> 00:49:36,932
We kept getting those messages.

1103
00:49:37,016 --> 00:49:40,269
Something about that felt off,
so I didn't tag her.

1104
00:49:40,352 --> 00:49:41,729
I didn't tag her though.

1105
00:49:41,812 --> 00:49:42,855
[ZZONE] Good call.

1106
00:49:42,938 --> 00:49:44,690
[Jaegyun] Yeah, and then...

1107
00:49:44,773 --> 00:49:48,152
[host] In "Time Between Dogs and Wolves,"
the Seeker failed.

1108
00:49:48,235 --> 00:49:50,029
-[Joonsu] Nice!
-Great.

1109
00:49:51,238 --> 00:49:52,656
[Jaegyun] ...the Seeker mission
was revealed.

1110
00:49:52,740 --> 00:49:55,075
[Sanghyun]
So their goal was to get tagged, right?

1111
00:49:55,159 --> 00:49:56,702
-[ZZONE] Yes.
-[Sanghyun] To get incorrectly tagged?

1112
00:49:56,785 --> 00:49:58,662
[host] The players chosen
by the Seeker are...

1113
00:50:00,289 --> 00:50:01,332
Hwang Jaegyun...

1114
00:50:03,042 --> 00:50:04,210
[Jaegyun] I was convinced it was Jimin.

1115
00:50:04,293 --> 00:50:06,462
That's when I knew for sure.

1116
00:50:06,545 --> 00:50:08,506
That's why I voted for Jimin too.

1117
00:50:09,715 --> 00:50:13,552
There were clear reasons to suspect her,
not just from gut feelings.

1118
00:50:14,178 --> 00:50:17,056
[Sanghyun]
There are a lot of things that made sense.

1119
00:50:17,139 --> 00:50:20,809
Something just felt really off.
I got all these weird vibes from her.

1120
00:50:20,893 --> 00:50:23,187
I was convinced it was Jimin.

1121
00:50:23,771 --> 00:50:26,607
[host] Park Jimin,
please leave the area immediately

1122
00:50:27,107 --> 00:50:28,984
and follow the guards' instructions.

1123
00:50:29,568 --> 00:50:31,111
[groans] Seriously...

1124
00:50:33,030 --> 00:50:35,658
I was so close to making it.

1125
00:50:35,741 --> 00:50:36,742
God damn it.

1126
00:50:37,326 --> 00:50:40,996
It felt like being in a race
and falling 10 m short of the finish line.

1127
00:50:42,039 --> 00:50:43,165
[groans softly]

1128
00:50:44,291 --> 00:50:46,961
I was so close. It was such a shame.

1129
00:50:48,128 --> 00:50:49,797
[groans] Seriously.

1130
00:50:52,341 --> 00:50:54,009
[groans] This is so frustrating.

1131
00:50:56,554 --> 00:50:58,639
I just needed to hold out a little longer.

1132
00:50:59,682 --> 00:51:03,936
Come on, what the heck?
After going through all that?

1133
00:51:04,019 --> 00:51:05,521
This is so annoying.

1134
00:51:08,482 --> 00:51:10,693
[sighs] And so, it ends in prison.

1135
00:51:11,902 --> 00:51:14,029
Why the hell...

1136
00:51:16,574 --> 00:51:18,534
[Sanghyun] So is Deadly Tag over?
What happens now?

1137
00:51:18,617 --> 00:51:19,868
The Seeker has been caught.

1138
00:51:19,952 --> 00:51:22,454
-So Deadly Tag is over?
-[ZZONE snorts]

1139
00:51:22,538 --> 00:51:24,123
[mic feedback]

1140
00:51:24,206 --> 00:51:27,960
[host] Now, we will select a new Seeker.

1141
00:51:28,043 --> 00:51:29,169
[all exclaiming]

1142
00:51:29,253 --> 00:51:32,047
-[Jaegyun] What is wrong with them?
-[Horseking] Come on! Seriously?

1143
00:51:32,131 --> 00:51:34,717
They're going to pick a new Seeker.
[chuckles softly]

1144
00:51:34,800 --> 00:51:39,388
[groans] It's so frustrating
because there will be another Seeker!

1145
00:51:39,888 --> 00:51:42,600
[Horseking]
I think the mission for the Seeker

1146
00:51:42,683 --> 00:51:44,351
-was so hard.
-The mission was so hard.

1147
00:51:44,435 --> 00:51:45,561
[ZZONE] It must've been so hard.

1148
00:51:45,644 --> 00:51:47,062
[Sanghyun]
They played two games on their own.

1149
00:51:47,146 --> 00:51:48,230
-[Horseking] Exactly.
-[ZZONE] Yeah.

1150
00:51:48,314 --> 00:51:51,483
No, actually three.
They have to act when they're among us,

1151
00:51:51,567 --> 00:51:53,485
-win the Main Match...
-[Sanghyun] Right.

1152
00:51:53,569 --> 00:51:55,321
[Horseking]
...and do their own mission too.

1153
00:51:55,404 --> 00:51:56,822
[mic feedback]

1154
00:51:58,157 --> 00:52:00,951
[host] There is only one Seeker Vote left.

1155
00:52:01,702 --> 00:52:05,080
If the Seeker survives this final vote,

1156
00:52:05,873 --> 00:52:08,500
they advance to the finals,
regardless of Main Match results.

1157
00:52:08,584 --> 00:52:10,628
-[all exclaiming]
-[♪ exhilarating music playing]

1158
00:52:10,711 --> 00:52:12,921
[chuckling] That's like
winning the lottery.

1159
00:52:13,005 --> 00:52:14,256
Exactly.

1160
00:52:14,340 --> 00:52:18,385
For me, I'd rather be the Seeker.

1161
00:52:18,969 --> 00:52:23,098
Since I could go straight to the finals
regardless of the Main Match results,

1162
00:52:23,182 --> 00:52:25,142
it was very enticing.

1163
00:52:25,225 --> 00:52:27,186
[Dail] This Seeker gig
is a hell of a sweet deal.

1164
00:52:27,269 --> 00:52:28,812
I hope I get picked.

1165
00:52:28,896 --> 00:52:30,814
I wanted to get picked so badly.

1166
00:52:30,898 --> 00:52:33,233
I really want to be the Seeker just once.

1167
00:52:34,276 --> 00:52:36,153
But what if the Seeker gets caught?

1168
00:52:36,236 --> 00:52:37,529
-[ZZONE] They'd be done for.
-In that case...

1169
00:52:37,613 --> 00:52:39,365
-[ZZONE] Eliminated.
-...straight to the Death Match.

1170
00:52:39,448 --> 00:52:40,658
It may not be only a good thing.

1171
00:52:40,741 --> 00:52:42,034
-It's a gamble.
-[Joonsu] A gamble.

1172
00:52:42,576 --> 00:52:43,577
[ZZONE] Right.

1173
00:52:43,661 --> 00:52:44,662
[Jaegyun in English]
High return, high risk.

1174
00:52:44,745 --> 00:52:46,163
[Horseking in Korean]
No, I never want to be one.

1175
00:52:46,246 --> 00:52:49,917
I couldn't possibly become the Seeker.
I don't want to.

1176
00:52:50,000 --> 00:52:52,461
I'm a terrible liar.
I'll make it so obvious.

1177
00:52:52,544 --> 00:52:58,175
I'm just someone
who's not good at that kind of stuff.

1178
00:52:58,258 --> 00:53:00,386
I really did worry about that
and again thought,

1179
00:53:00,469 --> 00:53:02,763
"What if I go in there
and end up being the Seeker?"

1180
00:53:02,846 --> 00:53:04,932
Being the Seeker? No, thanks.

1181
00:53:05,015 --> 00:53:08,852
I got too much suspicion of being
the Seeker. It really stressed me out.

1182
00:53:09,353 --> 00:53:10,604
[sighs]

1183
00:53:10,688 --> 00:53:12,981
I can't multitask.

1184
00:53:13,065 --> 00:53:16,235
I have to focus during the Main Match.

1185
00:53:16,318 --> 00:53:18,904
But if I have the Seeker mission too,
I'd be so busy.

1186
00:53:18,987 --> 00:53:22,074
So I hope I don't get picked
as the Seeker.

1187
00:53:23,242 --> 00:53:24,368
I'll go first.

1188
00:53:24,451 --> 00:53:25,452
-[Jaegyun] Okay.
-[Horseking] I'm curious.

1189
00:53:25,536 --> 00:53:27,955
It's a one-in-eight chance,
so you likely won't be picked.

1190
00:53:28,038 --> 00:53:29,081
Statistically.

1191
00:53:29,915 --> 00:53:32,751
I'd still rather not get picked.

1192
00:53:36,046 --> 00:53:37,047
Seriously.

1193
00:53:37,881 --> 00:53:39,883
[♪ quirky music playing]

1194
00:53:41,468 --> 00:53:44,221
[dealer] Mr. Horseking,
please select a card and flip it over.

1195
00:53:44,805 --> 00:53:46,598
-[Horseking] I'll go with the last one.
-[dealer] Okay.

1196
00:53:46,682 --> 00:53:48,100
[murmurs] No way it'll be me.

1197
00:53:50,477 --> 00:53:52,688
[♪ quirky music turns intriguing]

1198
00:53:56,650 --> 00:53:58,152
You're kidding, right?

1199
00:53:59,486 --> 00:54:00,487
[exclaims]

1200
00:54:16,378 --> 00:54:17,379
[dealer] Please flip it over.

1201
00:54:21,216 --> 00:54:22,217
[gulps]

1202
00:54:24,762 --> 00:54:26,096
[exclaims, chuckles]

1203
00:54:33,395 --> 00:54:34,938
[giggling]

1204
00:54:35,022 --> 00:54:36,023
[in English] Nice!

1205
00:54:39,693 --> 00:54:41,695
[host in Korean]
The Seeker has been selected.

1206
00:54:44,198 --> 00:54:48,577
There is a Seeker among you.

1207
00:54:54,875 --> 00:54:56,293
Who could it be?

1208
00:54:56,376 --> 00:54:59,463
[ZZONE] I don't think you can predict
how things will play out now.

1209
00:55:01,423 --> 00:55:03,342
[Dail] The Seeker
will be so damn happy tomorrow.

1210
00:55:03,425 --> 00:55:04,718
-Horseking.
-[Horseking] Yeah?

1211
00:55:04,801 --> 00:55:06,220
-You're the Seeker, aren't you?
-Never.

1212
00:55:06,303 --> 00:55:07,596
[Dail chuckles]

1213
00:55:08,055 --> 00:55:10,265
[chuckling] Dail, why are you
looking at her like that?

1214
00:55:10,349 --> 00:55:11,558
[Sanghyun laughing] Dail.

1215
00:55:11,642 --> 00:55:12,893
-[Jaegyun] Dail...
-You're the Seeker, huh?

1216
00:55:12,976 --> 00:55:13,977
I wish I were the Seeker,

1217
00:55:14,061 --> 00:55:15,729
-considering the Main Match.
-You are.

1218
00:55:15,812 --> 00:55:17,856
We absolutely have to catch the Seeker.

1219
00:55:17,940 --> 00:55:19,983
So I kept an eye on everyone.

1220
00:55:20,567 --> 00:55:21,985
YANG DAIL OBSERVED THE OTHERS

1221
00:55:22,069 --> 00:55:23,070
[Sanghyun] The Seeker...

1222
00:55:23,904 --> 00:55:26,573
-It seems to drop by that amount.
-Yeah, eight.

1223
00:55:27,950 --> 00:55:30,077
I've finally found the Seeker.

1224
00:55:30,661 --> 00:55:32,996
-Ddolddol, you're the Seeker, aren't you?
-[Ddolddol] No.

1225
00:55:33,580 --> 00:55:36,500
-[Dail chuckling]
-Why? Are you testing me again?

1226
00:55:36,583 --> 00:55:37,584
[Dail] No, I'm not.

1227
00:55:37,668 --> 00:55:39,670
[♪ tense music playing]

1228
00:55:40,629 --> 00:55:41,964
You're acting different. [chuckles softly]

1229
00:55:42,047 --> 00:55:44,091
-[Ddolddol] You think so?
-[Dail snickers]

1230
00:55:44,174 --> 00:55:46,176
[both laughing]

1231
00:55:50,847 --> 00:55:54,476
Ddolddol told me something in prison.

1232
00:55:54,560 --> 00:55:56,937
Honestly, it's extremely hard for me
to lie to someone like him.

1233
00:55:57,020 --> 00:56:00,190
He's the type to ask you something
straight to your face.

1234
00:56:00,274 --> 00:56:02,359
I honestly thought
he'd caught on at the start.

1235
00:56:02,442 --> 00:56:03,443
[Pani Bottle exclaims]

1236
00:56:03,527 --> 00:56:05,612
But after we picked our cards...

1237
00:56:05,696 --> 00:56:08,156
I heard that before I went,
so I was unfazed.

1238
00:56:10,701 --> 00:56:11,827
There were no letters.

1239
00:56:11,910 --> 00:56:13,245
Right, no letters.

1240
00:56:14,079 --> 00:56:16,498
[Dail] He kept avoiding
eye contact with me.

1241
00:56:16,582 --> 00:56:20,085
That reminded me
of what we talked about in prison.

1242
00:56:21,295 --> 00:56:22,629
[exclaims]

1243
00:56:23,255 --> 00:56:24,298
"So it's you."

1244
00:56:24,881 --> 00:56:25,966
[♪ music stops]

1245
00:56:26,049 --> 00:56:27,301
[Sanghyun shudders, sighs]

1246
00:56:27,384 --> 00:56:30,721
[murmurs] I think it's Jaegyun.

1247
00:56:30,804 --> 00:56:32,806
[♪ slow tense music playing]

1248
00:56:34,600 --> 00:56:35,767
It's got to be Jaegyun.

1249
00:56:38,812 --> 00:56:40,689
Doesn't Jaegyun seem like the Seeker?

1250
00:56:42,691 --> 00:56:45,819
[Ddolddol] But is he a good liar?

1251
00:56:45,902 --> 00:56:47,446
Well, I guess there's no need to lie.

1252
00:56:47,529 --> 00:56:49,197
-You just need to be quiet.
-Yes, exactly.

1253
00:56:49,281 --> 00:56:51,199
I'm really suspicious of Jaegyun.

1254
00:56:51,283 --> 00:56:53,660
Because he seemed really restless.

1255
00:56:54,328 --> 00:56:57,623
His eyes kept moving back and forth,

1256
00:56:58,206 --> 00:57:01,209
he kept shaking legs,
and he was fidgeting with his fingers.

1257
00:57:02,002 --> 00:57:03,462
It was just not like him.

1258
00:57:03,545 --> 00:57:04,713
[♪ music stops]

1259
00:57:04,796 --> 00:57:06,340
[distorted voice]
As long as I complete my mission,

1260
00:57:06,423 --> 00:57:08,175
they shouldn't be able to find me.

1261
00:57:08,759 --> 00:57:11,136
DINING ROOM AFTER EVERYONE'S ASLEEP

1262
00:57:11,219 --> 00:57:13,221
[♪ ominous music playing]

1263
00:57:14,306 --> 00:57:17,392
[host] According to the rules
of Deadly Tag,

1264
00:57:17,976 --> 00:57:19,603
you have become the Seeker.

1265
00:57:19,686 --> 00:57:20,896
THE SECOND SEEKER ROOM OPENS

1266
00:57:22,230 --> 00:57:24,566
Please choose three players
who will be revealed

1267
00:57:24,650 --> 00:57:28,153
as excluded from Seeker candidates
if the Seeker mission is a failure.

1268
00:57:30,447 --> 00:57:32,032
[distorted voice] Can you find me?

1269
00:57:33,158 --> 00:57:34,618
Will you be able to figure it out?

1270
00:57:35,786 --> 00:57:38,038
Catch me if you can.

1271
00:57:38,789 --> 00:57:40,874
[host] Please gather in the Main Hall.

1272
00:57:40,957 --> 00:57:42,709
[♪ ominous music turns intriguing]

1273
00:57:42,834 --> 00:57:46,797
We will now reveal
the final Main Match of Deadly Tag.

1274
00:57:51,843 --> 00:57:56,223
Tomorrow's Main Match is "Rainbow Catch."

1275
00:57:57,307 --> 00:57:58,308
[in English] "Rainbow."

1276
00:57:58,392 --> 00:58:01,812
[host in Korean] "Rainbow Catch"
is a color-based game of tag

1277
00:58:01,895 --> 00:58:04,773
where the chaser and the chased
switch roles in real time

1278
00:58:04,856 --> 00:58:07,067
depending on the color combinations
formed by players.

1279
00:58:07,150 --> 00:58:08,568
Is it an individual competition?

1280
00:58:08,652 --> 00:58:10,070
It should be.

1281
00:58:10,153 --> 00:58:12,906
[host] "Rainbow Catch"
uses color combinations

1282
00:58:12,989 --> 00:58:14,700
based on the three primary colors.

1283
00:58:15,367 --> 00:58:19,162
Red, orange, yellow,
green, blue, and purple.

1284
00:58:19,246 --> 00:58:21,164
There are six colors in total.

1285
00:58:22,082 --> 00:58:24,960
Tagging order
follows the colors of the rainbow

1286
00:58:25,544 --> 00:58:27,337
in a rotating cycle.

1287
00:58:28,880 --> 00:58:32,884
Players can only tag the color
that comes immediately after their own.

1288
00:58:34,261 --> 00:58:37,264
Tagging any other color will not count.

1289
00:58:38,390 --> 00:58:42,060
A successful tag is worth five points,

1290
00:58:42,144 --> 00:58:45,230
while the tagged player
will lose five points.

1291
00:58:45,939 --> 00:58:49,151
So basically, we have to tag
in rainbow color order.

1292
00:58:49,234 --> 00:58:50,444
-Right.
-[Jaegyun] Tag only the next color.

1293
00:58:50,527 --> 00:58:51,737
Like a chain.

1294
00:58:52,320 --> 00:58:54,823
[host] This game
will consist of two rounds.

1295
00:58:54,906 --> 00:58:56,700
Round 1 will last 30 minutes.

1296
00:58:56,783 --> 00:58:58,618
Round 2 will last 60 minutes.

1297
00:59:00,495 --> 00:59:03,373
Each round
consists of the Color Selection phase

1298
00:59:03,874 --> 00:59:05,959
and the Color Tag phase.

1299
00:59:06,626 --> 00:59:10,005
In the Color Selection phase,
players can choose from three colors.

1300
00:59:10,088 --> 00:59:13,175
Red, yellow, and blue.

1301
00:59:13,258 --> 00:59:17,387
Up to three players
can select the same color.

1302
00:59:17,929 --> 00:59:19,890
The card you select

1303
00:59:19,973 --> 00:59:23,643
becomes your starting color
in the Color Tag phase.

1304
00:59:23,727 --> 00:59:25,604
During the Color Tag phase,

1305
00:59:25,687 --> 00:59:29,274
players can collect color cards
and special cards hidden around the area.

1306
00:59:29,357 --> 00:59:33,653
You can combine the color cards
you collect to change your own color

1307
00:59:33,737 --> 00:59:36,531
or even change another player's color.

1308
00:59:37,115 --> 00:59:38,742
-[Dail] Mmm...
-[Horseking] Hmm...

1309
00:59:39,576 --> 00:59:42,954
[host] All item cards can be exchanged
or transferred to other players.

1310
00:59:43,830 --> 00:59:47,793
There are also White Cards
in "Rainbow Catch."

1311
00:59:48,543 --> 00:59:51,797
Here is how a player
turns into a White Card.

1312
00:59:52,589 --> 00:59:55,425
When a player is tagged,
they must go to the Black and White Zone

1313
00:59:55,509 --> 00:59:57,177
and stay in isolation for two minutes.

1314
00:59:57,761 --> 01:00:01,014
After two minutes of isolation,
they return to the game as a White Card

1315
01:00:01,097 --> 01:00:03,433
with no color for five minutes.

1316
01:00:04,100 --> 01:00:08,021
During this time, a White Card
can tag players of any color.

1317
01:00:08,730 --> 01:00:09,731
What?

1318
01:00:10,816 --> 01:00:13,485
[host] If a White Card tags someone
within those five minutes,

1319
01:00:13,568 --> 01:00:16,613
they take that player's color
and continue chasing.

1320
01:00:18,657 --> 01:00:21,868
If they fail to tag anyone,
they are eliminated from that round.

1321
01:00:23,286 --> 01:00:25,956
Even if a White Card successfully
tags someone, they do not earn any points.

1322
01:00:26,039 --> 01:00:27,541
they do not earn any points.

1323
01:00:27,624 --> 01:00:30,293
Only the tagged player loses five points.

1324
01:00:30,961 --> 01:00:34,005
This mission will definitely require
some athleticism too.

1325
01:00:34,089 --> 01:00:35,590
So the one with the most tags...

1326
01:00:35,674 --> 01:00:36,883
-We need to do it.
-[Sanghyun] ...wins.

1327
01:00:36,967 --> 01:00:38,301
[Ddolddol]
It's basically a battle of athleticism.

1328
01:00:38,385 --> 01:00:41,054
[Dail] I'm going to have to run
like crazy tomorrow.

1329
01:00:41,137 --> 01:00:43,932
You get five points for tagging someone,

1330
01:00:44,015 --> 01:00:46,017
but if you get tagged, you lose five.

1331
01:00:46,101 --> 01:00:48,144
And if you hit minus five, you turn white

1332
01:00:48,228 --> 01:00:51,481
and have to tag someone to get back in.

1333
01:00:51,565 --> 01:00:53,692
But that tag doesn't count for points.

1334
01:00:53,775 --> 01:00:57,904
So in a nutshell, getting tagged
means losing points and doing extra work.

1335
01:00:58,488 --> 01:01:02,075
I'm going to have to run like crazy again.

1336
01:01:02,993 --> 01:01:04,244
[host] At the end of each round,

1337
01:01:04,327 --> 01:01:06,830
players who don't survive
lose five points,

1338
01:01:07,539 --> 01:01:10,750
while those who do survive
earn five points.

1339
01:01:11,960 --> 01:01:15,171
Scores from each round will be added up
to determine the rankings.

1340
01:01:15,255 --> 01:01:19,301
Two finalists will be determined first
based on the rules.

1341
01:01:19,384 --> 01:01:20,552
[exclaims softly]

1342
01:01:20,635 --> 01:01:21,720
[exclaims]

1343
01:01:21,803 --> 01:01:25,515
The final number of finalists
will be revealed tomorrow.

1344
01:01:26,600 --> 01:01:29,311
So only the top two move on
and the rest go to the Death Match?

1345
01:01:29,394 --> 01:01:30,395
-[Horseking] Yes.
-[ZZONE] Right.

1346
01:01:30,478 --> 01:01:33,398
But the Seeker will advance.

1347
01:01:33,481 --> 01:01:34,482
[Ddolddol] Right.

1348
01:01:34,566 --> 01:01:35,567
I know.

1349
01:01:35,650 --> 01:01:39,905
THE SEEKER IS STILL OUT THERE

1350
01:01:40,572 --> 01:01:42,157
[Ddolddol]
Studying the Main Match tomorrow?

1351
01:01:42,240 --> 01:01:43,241
[Junseo] Yes.

1352
01:01:43,325 --> 01:01:44,367
MEN'S QUARTERS
AFTER MAIN MATCH ANNOUNCEMENT

1353
01:01:44,451 --> 01:01:47,329
[Ddolddol] You know how we could pull
a little trick? Want me to tell you?

1354
01:01:47,412 --> 01:01:48,413
[Junseo] Yes, please.

1355
01:01:48,496 --> 01:01:50,206
[Ddolddol] A team of three
would be fucking strong.

1356
01:01:50,290 --> 01:01:51,291
[Junseo] Really?

1357
01:01:51,374 --> 01:01:53,960
[Ddolddol]
Everyone will be scrambling for cards,

1358
01:01:54,419 --> 01:01:55,921
but if we collect item cards together,

1359
01:01:56,004 --> 01:01:57,589
-that'd put us ahead.
-[Junseo] Mmm...

1360
01:01:57,672 --> 01:02:00,133
If you think about it,
through color combinations,

1361
01:02:00,216 --> 01:02:02,135
we could go from red to orange.

1362
01:02:02,218 --> 01:02:04,971
Or I could pick a player

1363
01:02:05,055 --> 01:02:08,266
and change their color.

1364
01:02:08,350 --> 01:02:10,852
[inhales sharply]
I think we could make alliances.

1365
01:02:10,936 --> 01:02:13,188
-It's based on the three primary colors.
-Yeah.

1366
01:02:13,271 --> 01:02:15,815
If we're a trio, think about it.
Red, yellow, and blue.

1367
01:02:15,899 --> 01:02:17,400
-[Sanghyun] We each take one?
-Yes.

1368
01:02:17,484 --> 01:02:20,737
-If we each get red, yellow, and blue...
-Right, since we can trade items.

1369
01:02:20,820 --> 01:02:22,530
We agreed to share our items first.

1370
01:02:22,614 --> 01:02:24,991
If we have red, yellow, blue, we're safe.

1371
01:02:25,075 --> 01:02:28,078
The three of us can stick together
on one floor, keep each other safe,

1372
01:02:28,161 --> 01:02:31,331
and protect each other if someone attacks.

1373
01:02:31,414 --> 01:02:34,751
Since the game is based
on tailing each other,

1374
01:02:34,834 --> 01:02:38,546
the people you have to tag
will change in real time.

1375
01:02:38,630 --> 01:02:40,090
I figured it'd be better to have

1376
01:02:40,173 --> 01:02:42,676
someone on my side
instead of having everyone against me.

1377
01:02:42,759 --> 01:02:44,719
[Ddolddol] So early on,
we help each other not get tagged.

1378
01:02:44,803 --> 01:02:46,554
And focus on collecting some items?

1379
01:02:47,847 --> 01:02:49,641
[Jaegyun] Tomorrow's for sure
an individual competition.

1380
01:02:49,724 --> 01:02:50,976
[Joonsu] Only the top two
avoid the Death Match?

1381
01:02:51,059 --> 01:02:52,060
Yeah.

1382
01:02:52,143 --> 01:02:55,772
That's why I think
alliances won't matter tomorrow.

1383
01:02:55,855 --> 01:02:57,190
[Horseking] You have to go solo.

1384
01:02:57,273 --> 01:03:02,320
Alliances will be hard to keep
since we all need red, yellow, and blue.

1385
01:03:02,404 --> 01:03:03,780
How can you even team up?

1386
01:03:03,863 --> 01:03:07,200
Right? How will you change
someone's color? Let them tag you?

1387
01:03:07,283 --> 01:03:09,619
The most we can really do

1388
01:03:09,703 --> 01:03:12,330
is swap colors with each other...

1389
01:03:12,414 --> 01:03:16,251
And give someone a color if we happen to
have one they need. That's about it.

1390
01:03:16,334 --> 01:03:17,460
[Dail] Yeah, that's about it.

1391
01:03:17,544 --> 01:03:18,837
SOME ARE SKEPTICAL ABOUT ALLIANCES

1392
01:03:19,421 --> 01:03:23,466
This was clearly a solo game.

1393
01:03:23,550 --> 01:03:26,553
Even with an alliance, it'd still be hard
to finish first or second.

1394
01:03:26,636 --> 01:03:29,389
There wasn't really much to gain.

1395
01:03:29,472 --> 01:03:32,392
On top of that,
I was pretty confident in my running.

1396
01:03:32,475 --> 01:03:35,020
The wrong alliance
could turn on you at any second.

1397
01:03:35,103 --> 01:03:38,440
I might take out my own ally
if that's what it takes to advance.

1398
01:03:38,523 --> 01:03:40,483
So, I figured it's better to play solo.

1399
01:03:41,067 --> 01:03:42,360
[Jaegyun]
I really want to be first or second.

1400
01:03:42,444 --> 01:03:43,445
[Horseking] Oh, yeah?

1401
01:03:43,528 --> 01:03:46,072
[Dail] Tomorrow, I'm going to run
as if my life depends on it.

1402
01:03:48,491 --> 01:03:50,493
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

1403
01:03:59,085 --> 01:04:00,920
[ZZONE exclaims] Unbelievable.

1404
01:04:01,004 --> 01:04:02,213
[Joonsu] This place is crazy.

1405
01:04:02,797 --> 01:04:04,424
-[Horseking] It's so huge.
-[Joonsu] What?

1406
01:04:04,507 --> 01:04:07,302
[Dail] This wasn't some small company.
A major corporation was here.

1407
01:04:07,385 --> 01:04:09,095
[Joonsu] How did they even get this place?

1408
01:04:15,685 --> 01:04:17,228
It looks so nice.

1409
01:04:17,312 --> 01:04:18,438
-Look at the building.
-[ZZONE] I know.

1410
01:04:18,521 --> 01:04:20,857
I haven't seen
a normal-looking building in a while.

1411
01:04:20,940 --> 01:04:24,527
[host] The "Rainbow Catch" chase area
has four levels,

1412
01:04:24,986 --> 01:04:27,322
from the basement to the third floor.

1413
01:04:27,405 --> 01:04:28,573
The basement.

1414
01:04:29,199 --> 01:04:31,117
-[Sanghyun] You won't find hiders here.
-It's impossible.

1415
01:04:31,201 --> 01:04:32,410
AN AREA GOOD FOR HIDING

1416
01:04:32,494 --> 01:04:34,621
-[host] The first floor.
-[ZZONE] Why's everything so wide open?

1417
01:04:34,704 --> 01:04:36,247
There's nowhere to hide here.

1418
01:04:36,331 --> 01:04:38,208
AN OPEN SPACE OPTIMIZED
FOR HIGH-SPEED CHASES

1419
01:04:38,291 --> 01:04:39,334
[host] The second floor.

1420
01:04:39,417 --> 01:04:41,669
-[Jaegyun] We're in trouble.
-[Joonsu] It's like a maze.

1421
01:04:41,753 --> 01:04:42,921
A MAZE-LIKE SPACE

1422
01:04:43,755 --> 01:04:45,590
-[host] The third floor.
-[Jaegyun] This must be for bosses.

1423
01:04:45,673 --> 01:04:46,758
[Horseking] The chairman's office.

1424
01:04:47,509 --> 01:04:48,635
[Sanghyun] I feel dizzy.

1425
01:04:48,718 --> 01:04:50,720
-[Jaegyun] It's too big.
-[Sanghyun] Everything looks the same.

1426
01:04:51,763 --> 01:04:53,223
What on earth is this place?

1427
01:04:53,306 --> 01:04:55,350
It's hard to figure out the layout.

1428
01:04:55,433 --> 01:04:56,684
DOZENS OF ROOMS

1429
01:04:56,768 --> 01:05:00,688
There are way too many rooms,
and there are more than 100 hiding spots.

1430
01:05:00,772 --> 01:05:02,065
A MAZE-LIKE LAYOUT

1431
01:05:02,148 --> 01:05:05,026
You could get caught
just going around opening this and that.

1432
01:05:05,110 --> 01:05:06,861
Even a weaker player

1433
01:05:06,945 --> 01:05:10,824
can make it pretty far in this game
if they hide well.

1434
01:05:10,907 --> 01:05:12,742
Okay, this is not bad.

1435
01:05:13,535 --> 01:05:17,914
[host] There is one Dealer Room
on each of the second and third floors.

1436
01:05:17,997 --> 01:05:22,085
And there are three special areas
on the first floor.

1437
01:05:22,168 --> 01:05:23,586
The Card Selection Zone,

1438
01:05:24,754 --> 01:05:26,089
the Isolation Zone,

1439
01:05:27,799 --> 01:05:29,300
and the Black and White Zone.

1440
01:05:29,384 --> 01:05:31,386
[♪ tense music playing]

1441
01:05:31,928 --> 01:05:35,306
All players, please gather
in the Black and White Zone.

1442
01:05:36,641 --> 01:05:38,184
[Jaegyun]
So this is the Black and White Zone.

1443
01:05:38,268 --> 01:05:39,602
[ZZONE] This place is so scary.

1444
01:05:39,686 --> 01:05:41,563
[Joonsu] I feel like
I'm going to lose my mind.

1445
01:05:42,147 --> 01:05:43,398
[Sanghyun] There are many hiding spots.

1446
01:05:43,481 --> 01:05:45,775
-[Horseking] You're a master at hiding.
-[mic feedback]

1447
01:05:46,901 --> 01:05:50,780
[host] Before we begin this match,
we have an important announcement.

1448
01:05:51,906 --> 01:05:56,286
In today's Main Match, two players
will secure their spots in the finals.

1449
01:05:57,203 --> 01:06:00,373
The number of players who will advance
to the finals through the Death Match

1450
01:06:01,875 --> 01:06:03,001
is three.

1451
01:06:03,877 --> 01:06:05,003
[Dail] Three people.

1452
01:06:05,086 --> 01:06:06,713
That's three out of seven.

1453
01:06:06,796 --> 01:06:09,048
[host] With two winners
from the Main Match

1454
01:06:09,799 --> 01:06:11,593
and three survivors from the Death Match,

1455
01:06:11,676 --> 01:06:15,221
a total of five players
will advance to the finals.

1456
01:06:15,305 --> 01:06:16,306
Five people.

1457
01:06:16,806 --> 01:06:20,727
I never want to be
in the Death Match again.

1458
01:06:20,810 --> 01:06:24,689
I'll do whatever it takes
to win the Main Match.

1459
01:06:25,732 --> 01:06:27,400
It feels like this
is going to be a dogfight.

1460
01:06:28,151 --> 01:06:30,737
[host] Players can enter
the Card Selection Zone

1461
01:06:31,279 --> 01:06:34,782
and choose one of nine cards.

1462
01:06:34,866 --> 01:06:35,867
RED, YELLOW

1463
01:06:35,950 --> 01:06:39,495
The cards are numbered
from one to nine on the back.

1464
01:06:40,079 --> 01:06:42,498
Starting with the lowest number,

1465
01:06:42,582 --> 01:06:45,126
players will enter the area
in one-minute intervals.

1466
01:06:46,294 --> 01:06:47,795
[Sanghyun] Then, number one is the best.

1467
01:06:48,504 --> 01:06:51,466
[host] You will have 30 minutes
to choose your card for Round 1.

1468
01:06:52,217 --> 01:06:54,510
The Card Selection Zone will open shortly.

1469
01:06:54,594 --> 01:06:58,056
Cards will be chosen
on a first-come, first-served basis.

1470
01:06:58,139 --> 01:06:59,515
First-come, first-served.

1471
01:07:07,232 --> 01:07:10,068
The chase is now on. Bye!

1472
01:07:10,151 --> 01:07:12,153
[all laughing]

1473
01:07:14,614 --> 01:07:17,492
[host] The Card Selection Zone
is now open.

1474
01:07:17,575 --> 01:07:19,160
[♪ music fades]

1475
01:07:19,244 --> 01:07:21,454
READING THE ROOM

1476
01:07:22,038 --> 01:07:24,540
-You want to go first, Sanghyun?
-I think I'm good.

1477
01:07:24,624 --> 01:07:26,292
-[ZZONE chuckles]
-You got here first.

1478
01:07:27,502 --> 01:07:29,087
-I'm scared.
-[Jaegyun] Why?

1479
01:07:29,170 --> 01:07:30,964
-[Horseking chuckles]
-I have a bad feeling.

1480
01:07:31,047 --> 01:07:32,340
[♪ quirky music plays, fades]

1481
01:07:32,423 --> 01:07:34,259
-I'll just go first then.
-[Sanghyun] All right.

1482
01:07:34,926 --> 01:07:38,388
YANG DAIL ENTERS THE CARD SELECTION ZONE

1483
01:07:38,471 --> 01:07:40,098
[♪ intriguing music playing]

1484
01:07:40,181 --> 01:07:42,809
Mr. Yang Dail, please select a color card.

1485
01:07:44,018 --> 01:07:46,187
[Dail sighs deeply]

1486
01:07:46,271 --> 01:07:48,856
I need to win this to get to the finals.

1487
01:07:48,940 --> 01:07:52,110
And just my luck, I hurt my toe

1488
01:07:52,193 --> 01:07:53,736
on a show where I have to run.

1489
01:07:55,196 --> 01:07:56,823
-[Ddolddol exclaims]
-[Jimin] Oh, my gosh.

1490
01:07:56,906 --> 01:07:59,200
DAIL GOT INJURED
AFTER TAGGING JUNSEO IN "KINGMAKER"

1491
01:07:59,284 --> 01:08:01,077
[Dail] I definitely have to run.

1492
01:08:01,160 --> 01:08:04,080
I knew I had to keep my head in the game.

1493
01:08:04,163 --> 01:08:05,832
So, I kept weighing my options.

1494
01:08:05,915 --> 01:08:09,085
THINKING CAREFULLY

1495
01:08:09,794 --> 01:08:11,129
-[murmurs] I'll go with red.
-[dealer] Okay.

1496
01:08:11,879 --> 01:08:14,465
-You have chosen the red card.
-[Dail] Yes.

1497
01:08:14,549 --> 01:08:16,426
-[dealer] Your number is one.
-[Dail] Goodness.

1498
01:08:16,509 --> 01:08:20,263
Luckily, I got number one,
so I thought I was off to a good start.

1499
01:08:21,472 --> 01:08:22,473
Hello.

1500
01:08:22,557 --> 01:08:25,393
Mr. Youn Sanghyun,
please select a color card.

1501
01:08:27,020 --> 01:08:30,106
You have chosen the yellow 2 card.

1502
01:08:30,690 --> 01:08:33,526
[Sanghyun] I actually had a card
I promised to pick.

1503
01:08:34,986 --> 01:08:36,279
I think sharing the information

1504
01:08:36,362 --> 01:08:37,739
-is awesome.
-[Ddolddol] Yes.

1505
01:08:37,822 --> 01:08:39,699
[Sanghyun] Why don't we decide first?

1506
01:08:40,283 --> 01:08:41,701
Want to assign red, yellow, and blue?

1507
01:08:41,784 --> 01:08:44,495
The three of us should decide
who will take which color.

1508
01:08:44,579 --> 01:08:46,622
[Junseo] I see. Sounds good.

1509
01:08:46,706 --> 01:08:50,418
[Sanghyun]
Then, we should make a group chat.

1510
01:08:50,501 --> 01:08:51,753
-[Ddolddol] Yeah.
-[Junseo] Let's do that.

1511
01:08:51,836 --> 01:08:54,464
[Sanghyun] So, we share the information
in that group chat only.

1512
01:08:54,547 --> 01:08:56,132
Then, we'll go tag them together.

1513
01:08:56,924 --> 01:08:59,010
We figured we'd become targets

1514
01:08:59,093 --> 01:09:01,763
if people knew we were in an alliance
from the start.

1515
01:09:03,639 --> 01:09:05,516
So, we made a group chat just for us.

1516
01:09:06,392 --> 01:09:07,435
RED, YELLOW, BLUE ALLIANCE

1517
01:09:07,518 --> 01:09:09,937
SANGHYUN
DON'T GET THE GROUP CHAT MIXED UP

1518
01:09:10,021 --> 01:09:11,731
JUNSEO
OKAY

1519
01:09:11,814 --> 01:09:13,816
DDOLDDOL
I'M BLUE, JUNSEO'S RED, SANGHYUN'S YELLOW?

1520
01:09:13,900 --> 01:09:15,193
OKAY
LET'S DO THAT

1521
01:09:15,276 --> 01:09:18,738
In the group chat,
we decided which color we should pick.

1522
01:09:18,821 --> 01:09:21,115
[dealer] You have chosen the red 7 card.

1523
01:09:22,367 --> 01:09:24,327
You have chosen the blue card.

1524
01:09:24,911 --> 01:09:26,204
[Horseking]
It's an individual competition.

1525
01:09:26,287 --> 01:09:29,207
It's an individual competition
since there are only two winners.

1526
01:09:29,290 --> 01:09:30,833
[Sanghyun] Going solo is the way to go.

1527
01:09:31,376 --> 01:09:34,003
We tried our best
not to show we had an alliance.

1528
01:09:37,006 --> 01:09:43,971
ROUND 1 CARD SELECTIONS

1529
01:09:46,349 --> 01:09:50,019
[host] The Color Tag phase will begin now.

1530
01:09:50,103 --> 01:09:51,771
[♪ rock music playing]

1531
01:09:52,063 --> 01:09:55,066
Hidden throughout the area
are white envelopes with color cards...

1532
01:09:57,318 --> 01:09:59,987
and black envelopes
containing special cards.

1533
01:10:01,906 --> 01:10:05,034
You may now begin to collect cards freely.

1534
01:10:05,535 --> 01:10:06,744
DEALER ROOM
OPEN

1535
01:10:06,828 --> 01:10:09,163
I'm scared!

1536
01:10:09,247 --> 01:10:10,248
[Joonsu in English] Holy, man!

1537
01:10:10,957 --> 01:10:13,376
[host in Korean]
Yang Dail has drawn the 1 card.

1538
01:10:13,459 --> 01:10:16,295
-We start right away, right?
-[host] Please enter the chase area.

1539
01:10:19,298 --> 01:10:22,885
[Dail] First, I need to find
as many color cards as I can

1540
01:10:22,969 --> 01:10:25,179
that will get me to my target color.

1541
01:10:27,140 --> 01:10:29,809
They made it hard as hell again.

1542
01:10:29,892 --> 01:10:32,103
Making it to the finals
is going to be tough.

1543
01:10:32,186 --> 01:10:34,021
Let's just keep going all the way.

1544
01:10:34,105 --> 01:10:36,941
[host] The second player, Youn Sanghyun.

1545
01:10:37,024 --> 01:10:39,485
[Sanghyun] I started running thinking,
"I have to win this."

1546
01:10:39,944 --> 01:10:42,238
[host] The third player, Lee Joonsu.

1547
01:10:42,321 --> 01:10:44,490
[Joonsu] I don't care who became what.

1548
01:10:47,577 --> 01:10:49,370
I just wanted to tag anyone.

1549
01:10:49,454 --> 01:10:52,415
[host] The fourth player, Hwang Jaegyun.

1550
01:10:53,207 --> 01:10:54,208
[Jaegyun] Where is it?

1551
01:10:56,294 --> 01:10:58,629
[host] The fifth player, ZZONE.

1552
01:11:00,923 --> 01:11:02,258
[Horseking] What could the mission be?

1553
01:11:02,967 --> 01:11:05,178
Maybe go to the Dealer Room
and change someone's color?

1554
01:11:05,261 --> 01:11:06,262
[Horseking exclaims]

1555
01:11:07,054 --> 01:11:08,181
That's very keen.

1556
01:11:08,264 --> 01:11:11,017
That's my guess.
Or it might not specify just one person.

1557
01:11:11,100 --> 01:11:13,060
[host] The sixth player, Horseking.

1558
01:11:13,144 --> 01:11:14,604
-[Horseking] Bye.
-[host] Please enter.

1559
01:11:14,687 --> 01:11:16,564
[♪ music fades]

1560
01:11:16,647 --> 01:11:20,860
[Ddolddol whispering] Dealer Room.
Go to the Dealer Room on the first floor.

1561
01:11:21,652 --> 01:11:23,029
Then, go straight to the stairs.

1562
01:11:23,112 --> 01:11:25,531
Climb up the stairs
to the third floor and browse.

1563
01:11:25,615 --> 01:11:27,158
Sanghyun will go up from the basement.

1564
01:11:27,241 --> 01:11:29,577
Go in there and scan this area.

1565
01:11:29,660 --> 01:11:32,371
I thought searching for items
would be important early on.

1566
01:11:32,455 --> 01:11:33,956
In our strategy, Sanghyun goes first,

1567
01:11:34,040 --> 01:11:37,251
looking for items in the basement
and then up through each floor.

1568
01:11:37,335 --> 01:11:39,962
Meanwhile, we'll head
straight to the third floor

1569
01:11:40,046 --> 01:11:42,799
and share locations of items
or card colors of players.

1570
01:11:42,882 --> 01:11:45,343
We promised to share
that information in real time.

1571
01:11:45,426 --> 01:11:48,429
[host] The seventh player, Yuk Junseo.

1572
01:11:48,513 --> 01:11:52,225
The last player, Kim Ddolddol,
please enter.

1573
01:11:52,308 --> 01:11:54,560
JUNSEO AND DDOLDDOL
ARRIVE AT 3RD FLOOR TO SEARCH

1574
01:11:55,353 --> 01:11:57,522
All players have entered.

1575
01:11:58,523 --> 01:12:00,399
You may now start tagging.

1576
01:12:06,531 --> 01:12:09,408
[Ddolddol] I was able to find
the item cards so easily.

1577
01:12:11,619 --> 01:12:13,496
I found a blue color card right away.

1578
01:12:13,579 --> 01:12:15,623
And another blue one.
I found two right away.

1579
01:12:15,706 --> 01:12:17,917
[♪ upbeat music playing]

1580
01:12:18,000 --> 01:12:19,794
DDOLDDOL
I FOUND BLUE, TWO BLUES

1581
01:12:20,711 --> 01:12:24,298
[Sanghyun] Following the plan I made
with Ddolddol and Junseo,

1582
01:12:25,341 --> 01:12:27,718
I started searching from the basement.

1583
01:12:36,561 --> 01:12:37,895
JUNSEO
I GOT 1 YELLOW, 1 BLUE

1584
01:12:37,979 --> 01:12:40,147
SANGHYUN
I GOT TWO REDS

1585
01:12:40,231 --> 01:12:42,316
Our team was finding items so well.

1586
01:12:42,400 --> 01:12:43,860
"I got two color cards as well."

1587
01:12:43,943 --> 01:12:46,028
"I found two color cards."

1588
01:12:46,112 --> 01:12:47,947
Oh my, I can't believe this.
It's going so well.

1589
01:12:52,869 --> 01:12:54,871
[♪ music stops]

1590
01:12:54,954 --> 01:12:55,955
[Sanghyun] Did you find any?

1591
01:12:56,038 --> 01:12:57,415
-[ZZONE] No, did you?
-[Sanghyun] Nope.

1592
01:12:57,498 --> 01:12:59,709
-[ZZONE] There aren't any, right?
-[Sanghyun] I found one,

1593
01:13:00,126 --> 01:13:01,419
but it's not the color I want.

1594
01:13:01,502 --> 01:13:02,628
[ZZONE] Which floor was it?

1595
01:13:03,296 --> 01:13:05,756
[Sanghyun] In the basement.
Let's go to the third floor.

1596
01:13:06,215 --> 01:13:07,425
[ZZONE] Mmm...

1597
01:13:07,508 --> 01:13:08,634
[pants] This is so tiring.

1598
01:13:09,135 --> 01:13:12,555
I ran into Sanghyun then
and checked his color.

1599
01:13:12,638 --> 01:13:13,890
He had a yellow card.

1600
01:13:13,973 --> 01:13:17,768
Sanghyun and Horseking
both had a yellow one.

1601
01:13:17,852 --> 01:13:19,896
And they're very strong physically.

1602
01:13:19,979 --> 01:13:22,940
So, I thought I had to team up
with the strong players.

1603
01:13:23,608 --> 01:13:24,609
[Sanghyun] Where's the Dealer Room?

1604
01:13:24,692 --> 01:13:26,277
[ZZONE]
The Dealer Room is on the second floor.

1605
01:13:26,819 --> 01:13:28,821
-[Sanghyun] It's also on the third floor.
-[ZZONE] Yes, it's both.

1606
01:13:28,905 --> 01:13:30,698
ZZONE & SANGHYUN
COME TO 3RD FLOOR TO SEARCH

1607
01:13:30,781 --> 01:13:32,366
-[Sanghyun] Here.
-[ZZONE] Yeah.

1608
01:13:32,450 --> 01:13:33,868
[Sanghyun]
I feel like it's near the Dealer Room.

1609
01:13:33,951 --> 01:13:34,994
[ZZONE] I think so too.

1610
01:13:35,077 --> 01:13:36,829
[Sanghyun] Yeah. It's over here, ZZONE.

1611
01:13:36,913 --> 01:13:38,915
[♪ stealthy music builds]

1612
01:13:40,875 --> 01:13:42,543
ZZONE FOLLOWS HIM

1613
01:13:43,044 --> 01:13:44,045
[ZZONE] This is exhausting.

1614
01:13:50,259 --> 01:13:52,261
[Sanghyun] ZZONE.

1615
01:13:52,345 --> 01:13:53,346
[ZZONE] Yeah?

1616
01:13:53,429 --> 01:13:54,722
Did you find anything?

1617
01:13:55,556 --> 01:13:56,933
[ZZONE] Mmm...

1618
01:13:57,016 --> 01:13:59,101
[♪ music fades]

1619
01:14:00,227 --> 01:14:05,691
SANGHYUN SUDDENLY GOES
SOMEWHERE BY HIMSELF

1620
01:14:05,775 --> 01:14:09,403
DEALER ROOM

1621
01:14:10,029 --> 01:14:12,239
[dealer] Please submit the card
you would like to register.

1622
01:14:12,949 --> 01:14:14,116
Could you mix them, please?

1623
01:14:14,659 --> 01:14:17,662
[dealer] Your yellow and red cards
will be combined

1624
01:14:17,745 --> 01:14:19,622
to make an orange card.

1625
01:14:20,247 --> 01:14:23,292
I picked up two red cards.

1626
01:14:23,793 --> 01:14:25,044
And my original card was yellow.

1627
01:14:25,127 --> 01:14:27,630
And ZZONE was there with me
holding a yellow card.

1628
01:14:27,713 --> 01:14:32,259
So I figured I should use the red card
to make an orange one

1629
01:14:32,885 --> 01:14:36,305
so that I can tag ZZONE with ease.

1630
01:14:37,306 --> 01:14:38,307
Where's the Dealer Room?

1631
01:14:38,391 --> 01:14:39,392
Here.

1632
01:14:40,059 --> 01:14:41,894
-Yeah.
-I feel like it's near the Dealer Room.

1633
01:14:41,978 --> 01:14:43,020
DEALER ROOM

1634
01:14:43,104 --> 01:14:44,105
[ZZONE] I think so too.

1635
01:14:44,188 --> 01:14:46,148
[Sanghyun] Yeah. It's over here, ZZONE.

1636
01:14:46,691 --> 01:14:47,900
It should be somewhere here.

1637
01:14:47,984 --> 01:14:49,068
HE LURES ZZONE TO DEALER ROOM

1638
01:14:49,151 --> 01:14:50,277
The Dealer Room is here.

1639
01:14:51,153 --> 01:14:52,154
It's at the end.

1640
01:14:52,238 --> 01:14:54,240
[♪ upbeat music playing]

1641
01:14:55,449 --> 01:14:56,450
Thank you.

1642
01:15:00,746 --> 01:15:01,872
[ZZONE] What's this?

1643
01:15:02,915 --> 01:15:03,916
[grunts]

1644
01:15:05,668 --> 01:15:10,756
MEANWHILE, ZZONE IS FOCUSED
ON FINDING ITEMS

1645
01:15:11,632 --> 01:15:12,717
-[Sanghyun] ZZONE.
-[ZZONE] Yeah?

1646
01:15:14,593 --> 01:15:16,554
-[Sanghyun] Did you find anything?
-[ZZONE] No. [exclaims]

1647
01:15:16,929 --> 01:15:18,389
-[Sanghyun] What did you find?
-[ZZONE] I found yellow.

1648
01:15:18,472 --> 01:15:19,807
-[Sanghyun] Yellow?
-[ZZONE] What do you have?

1649
01:15:19,890 --> 01:15:22,143
-What have you got?
-[Sanghyun] Nothing else here?

1650
01:15:22,768 --> 01:15:23,894
[ZZONE] You have an orange now.

1651
01:15:23,978 --> 01:15:25,229
-[host] Tag confirmed.
-[ZZONE] Hey!

1652
01:15:25,312 --> 01:15:26,689
SANGHYUN TAGS ZZONE

1653
01:15:26,772 --> 01:15:27,773
That's so annoying.

1654
01:15:27,857 --> 01:15:30,651
SANGHYUN
ZZONE

1655
01:15:30,735 --> 01:15:34,321
[groans] When did you change it to orange?

1656
01:15:34,405 --> 01:15:35,740
[Sanghyun] Let's go.

1657
01:15:35,823 --> 01:15:37,450
[ZZONE] He kept telling me to follow him.

1658
01:15:37,533 --> 01:15:40,119
I did wonder
why he was telling me to follow him.

1659
01:15:40,703 --> 01:15:44,165
He went to the Dealer Room
really quickly and tagged me.

1660
01:15:44,248 --> 01:15:46,333
I felt really betrayed.

1661
01:15:46,417 --> 01:15:48,169
Once I become a White Card,

1662
01:15:48,252 --> 01:15:50,546
I'll find Sanghyun by his voice
and get my revenge.

1663
01:15:51,464 --> 01:15:52,465
TAGGED PLAYERS ARE ISOLATED

1664
01:15:52,548 --> 01:15:54,008
IN BLACK AND WHITE ZONE FOR 2 MINUTES

1665
01:15:54,091 --> 01:15:55,092
I'm so annoyed.

1666
01:15:56,135 --> 01:15:59,430
ISOLATION STARTS

1667
01:15:59,513 --> 01:16:01,098
[groans] I'll get him, no matter what.

1668
01:16:03,726 --> 01:16:08,189
I earned five points, so I thought
I should keep up the momentum early on.

1669
01:16:08,272 --> 01:16:09,273
[♪ music stops]

1670
01:16:09,356 --> 01:16:11,108
SANGHYUN: YOU GOT BLUE?
DDOLDDOL: YEAH, TWO

1671
01:16:11,192 --> 01:16:12,193
SANGHYUN
TRADE FOR MY RED

1672
01:16:12,276 --> 01:16:13,527
DDOLDDOL
GO TO 3RD FLOOR DEALER ROOM

1673
01:16:14,820 --> 01:16:16,197
[Ddolddol whispering] Trade. Quick.

1674
01:16:17,907 --> 01:16:20,701
[Sanghyun] I should put someone safe
on the color chasing me.

1675
01:16:20,785 --> 01:16:22,453
[sighs] Blue.

1676
01:16:22,953 --> 01:16:25,247
[dealer] You have submitted a blue card.

1677
01:16:25,331 --> 01:16:27,875
Please name the player
you would like to use the card on.

1678
01:16:27,958 --> 01:16:29,168
[Sanghyun] Yang Dail.

1679
01:16:30,419 --> 01:16:31,420
-Yang Dail.
-[dealer] Yang Dail?

1680
01:16:31,504 --> 01:16:33,798
[Sanghyun]
I just had to avoid Dail and Junseo.

1681
01:16:33,881 --> 01:16:35,800
I didn't think Junseo would attack me.

1682
01:16:35,883 --> 01:16:37,760
[dealer] The red and blue will be combined

1683
01:16:37,843 --> 01:16:39,887
-to change the color to purple.
-[Sanghyun] Okay.

1684
01:16:39,970 --> 01:16:42,306
So with that thinking,
I turned Dail purple.

1685
01:16:43,516 --> 01:16:44,850
SOMEONE CHANGED YANG DAIL'S COLOR

1686
01:16:44,934 --> 01:16:46,852
PLEASE GO TO THE DEALER ROOM IMMEDIATELY

1687
01:16:46,936 --> 01:16:48,979
[Dail] What? Changed the color?

1688
01:16:50,439 --> 01:16:52,024
ANY PLAYER WHOSE COLOR HAS BEEN CHANGED

1689
01:16:52,108 --> 01:16:54,652
MUST IMMEDIATELY VISIT THE DEALER ROOM
TO UPDATE THEIR COLOR

1690
01:16:54,735 --> 01:16:55,778
[dealer] Mr. Yang Dail.

1691
01:16:56,612 --> 01:17:00,574
My color's been changed to purple
so blue cards can chase me.

1692
01:17:01,325 --> 01:17:05,037
All in all, Dail cannot tag me.

1693
01:17:05,121 --> 01:17:07,998
And Junseo wouldn't tag me.

1694
01:17:08,582 --> 01:17:10,417
So I could move around freely.

1695
01:17:10,501 --> 01:17:12,711
SANGHYUN HAS ALLY JUNSEO
BEHIND HIM ON RED

1696
01:17:12,795 --> 01:17:15,714
AND ENEMY IN FRONT OF HIM ON PURPLE

1697
01:17:17,007 --> 01:17:19,135
[♪ tense music playing]

1698
01:17:19,218 --> 01:17:21,428
I got changed from red to purple.

1699
01:17:21,512 --> 01:17:24,723
So, either a blue card
changed me to come after me,

1700
01:17:24,807 --> 01:17:28,310
or an orange card changed me,
so I wouldn't be able to tag them.

1701
01:17:30,312 --> 01:17:32,398
DEALER ROOM 1

1702
01:17:33,065 --> 01:17:35,359
DEALER ROOM 1

1703
01:17:38,195 --> 01:17:40,197
[♪ music fades]

1704
01:17:44,076 --> 01:17:46,328
Yuk Junseo's red,
and he's right in front of me.

1705
01:17:46,412 --> 01:17:47,538
Awesome.

1706
01:17:47,621 --> 01:17:49,623
[♪ rock music playing]

1707
01:17:53,669 --> 01:17:54,837
[grunts]

1708
01:17:56,505 --> 01:17:59,091
[grunts, exclaims]

1709
01:18:05,556 --> 01:18:09,435
YANG DAIL CHASES YUK JUNSEO

1710
01:18:09,518 --> 01:18:10,936
That hurts.

1711
01:18:20,070 --> 01:18:23,115
JUNSEO IS CORNERED

1712
01:18:23,199 --> 01:18:24,241
[♪ music fades]

1713
01:18:24,325 --> 01:18:25,701
-[Junseo panting] Let's team up.
-[Dail] What?

1714
01:18:25,784 --> 01:18:26,827
[Junseo] I'll help you.

1715
01:18:26,911 --> 01:18:30,998
I got him, but he asked me
to let him off and team up.

1716
01:18:31,081 --> 01:18:34,585
[laughing] I never expected Junseo
to do something like that.

1717
01:18:35,211 --> 01:18:36,837
[♪ comical music playing]

1718
01:18:36,921 --> 01:18:38,130
It was still early in the game,

1719
01:18:39,048 --> 01:18:44,678
and that wasn't really
going to make or break the game,

1720
01:18:44,762 --> 01:18:48,098
but I wanted to start
with at least one point.

1721
01:18:48,974 --> 01:18:49,975
[clicks tongue]

1722
01:18:52,269 --> 01:18:53,854
-I'll help you.
-[Dail] Team up?

1723
01:18:53,938 --> 01:18:55,773
[Junseo] Yes, I'll help you out.

1724
01:18:55,856 --> 01:18:56,899
[Dail] Okay.

1725
01:18:56,982 --> 01:18:59,026
[both panting]

1726
01:18:59,777 --> 01:19:03,781
YANG DAIL AND YUK JUNSEO
FORM A TEMPORARY ALLIANCE

1727
01:19:03,864 --> 01:19:07,910
Let's agree not to attack each other
if we cross paths.

1728
01:19:07,993 --> 01:19:09,870
[both huff]

1729
01:19:09,954 --> 01:19:12,665
Junseo is a strong player.

1730
01:19:12,748 --> 01:19:15,459
Having him on my side
makes things so much easier.

1731
01:19:15,542 --> 01:19:16,919
So, I let him off the hook.

1732
01:19:17,002 --> 01:19:18,087
[♪ music fades]

1733
01:19:18,170 --> 01:19:19,964
BASEMENT

1734
01:19:20,047 --> 01:19:21,090
[Jaegyun] Where are they?

1735
01:19:21,632 --> 01:19:23,634
[♪ eerie music playing]

1736
01:19:32,184 --> 01:19:33,185
[Horseking] Are they here?

1737
01:19:34,019 --> 01:19:35,312
Why did they put them here?

1738
01:19:40,526 --> 01:19:41,527
[Jaegyun] What's that?

1739
01:19:46,156 --> 01:19:48,158
[♪ music swells]

1740
01:19:50,744 --> 01:19:52,579
Hey, Horseking,
doesn't this look like a clue?

1741
01:19:52,663 --> 01:19:54,540
-[Horseking] What?
-Doesn't this look like a clue?

1742
01:20:01,922 --> 01:20:02,923
[Horseking] Huh?

1743
01:20:04,925 --> 01:20:05,968
You're right.

1744
01:20:06,051 --> 01:20:07,928
-[chuckling] There's a rainbow here.
-Right?

1745
01:20:08,012 --> 01:20:11,265
[Horseking] There was this huge door
with a lock on it,

1746
01:20:11,348 --> 01:20:14,310
and there was a rainbow-shaped clue
on the front of it.

1747
01:20:14,810 --> 01:20:16,854
Each color had letters on it.

1748
01:20:16,937 --> 01:20:19,732
And there was a lock, so it was a puzzle.

1749
01:20:19,815 --> 01:20:21,650
[♪ eerie music turns mysterious]

1750
01:20:21,734 --> 01:20:24,028
Here. From zero to nine.

1751
01:20:28,324 --> 01:20:30,492
Do you want to just break it? [chuckles]

1752
01:20:30,617 --> 01:20:32,619
[Jaegyun]
I feel like it'll lead us to something.

1753
01:20:36,832 --> 01:20:38,917
[Horseking] What are the letters for?
And the rainbow colors?

1754
01:20:39,001 --> 01:20:41,462
It must have something to do
with our card colors.

1755
01:20:42,880 --> 01:20:44,506
[Jaegyun murmurs in English] "Violet."

1756
01:20:46,467 --> 01:20:48,344
-[whispers] "Red. Red."
-[Jaegyun murmurs in Korean] Right.

1757
01:20:48,844 --> 01:20:50,846
-[in English] "Orange, yellow, green."
-"Orange."

1758
01:20:50,929 --> 01:20:52,473
[Jaegyun in Korean] Let's give it a try.

1759
01:20:52,556 --> 01:20:54,183
How do you spell "orange"?

1760
01:20:56,101 --> 01:21:00,022
It was red, so we thought "RED."
And sure enough, there were R, E, and D.

1761
01:21:00,105 --> 01:21:02,858
That had to be the clue.
So I said, "Let's take them out."

1762
01:21:02,941 --> 01:21:05,027
-[Jaegyun] In the middle...
-[Horseking] Let's take these out.

1763
01:21:05,110 --> 01:21:07,821
If we take out R, E, and D,
it spells "one."

1764
01:21:07,905 --> 01:21:09,531
-[Jaegyun] Right.
-[Horseking] "One."

1765
01:21:09,615 --> 01:21:10,741
HORSEKING FOUND THE KEY CLUE

1766
01:21:10,824 --> 01:21:12,576
If we take out "RED,"

1767
01:21:13,827 --> 01:21:15,287
we get "one."

1768
01:21:15,954 --> 01:21:19,166
So, the first one is "one."

1769
01:21:19,249 --> 01:21:23,170
Then, if we take out "orange,"
we get "eight."

1770
01:21:23,253 --> 01:21:25,005
Okay, next up is seven.

1771
01:21:25,089 --> 01:21:27,091
[♪ exhilarating music playing]

1772
01:21:38,894 --> 01:21:41,146
[whispering excitedly] We got it!
Oh, my gosh!

1773
01:21:42,523 --> 01:21:44,942
-We were right. We got it.
-Okay.

1774
01:21:46,652 --> 01:21:48,487
[♪ music fades]

1775
01:21:50,030 --> 01:21:51,198
What is this place?

1776
01:21:51,782 --> 01:21:53,367
-[Horseking] What is this place?
-What on earth?

1777
01:21:54,034 --> 01:21:56,370
[door creaking]

1778
01:21:56,453 --> 01:22:00,999
[Horseking] It was filled with smoke
with this light shining down from above.

1779
01:22:01,083 --> 01:22:04,420
And there was a wooden box
dangling from a single rope.

1780
01:22:06,004 --> 01:22:08,841
There had to be
something really good in that box.

1781
01:22:09,550 --> 01:22:10,968
-What is it?
-[Jaegyun] Wait.

1782
01:22:14,304 --> 01:22:16,515
[Horseking] What do you want to do?
Do you want to use it?

1783
01:22:17,933 --> 01:22:19,017
Can I?

1784
01:22:20,727 --> 01:22:22,312
[Horseking] Let's see what it is.

1785
01:22:24,815 --> 01:22:26,817
[♪ mysterious music playing]

1786
01:22:28,444 --> 01:22:29,445
[Horseking] On the back.

1787
01:22:30,195 --> 01:22:31,238
What is it?

1788
01:22:31,864 --> 01:22:32,865
It's a black card.

1789
01:22:32,948 --> 01:22:34,867
"For five minutes,
tag any color with no limit."

1790
01:22:35,451 --> 01:22:37,995
[host] The Black Card is a special card
that allows tagging

1791
01:22:38,078 --> 01:22:41,165
of any card color as many times
as desired for five minutes.

1792
01:22:41,248 --> 01:22:45,836
We've got the three primary colors,
red, yellow, and blue.

1793
01:22:45,919 --> 01:22:47,963
Then, green, orange, and purple.

1794
01:22:48,046 --> 01:22:50,674
And in the middle, there should be black.

1795
01:22:52,009 --> 01:22:56,263
I realized I absolutely needed this.

1796
01:22:56,346 --> 01:22:59,224
But I didn't know how to bring that up.

1797
01:22:59,308 --> 01:23:01,018
"What should I tell him so I can use it?"

1798
01:23:01,101 --> 01:23:03,228
That's what I kept thinking about.

1799
01:23:03,312 --> 01:23:05,731
-It's an incredible card, indeed.
-It's a great card.

1800
01:23:05,814 --> 01:23:07,274
-Then, let's do this.
-What?

1801
01:23:07,357 --> 01:23:09,067
Let's work together for now.

1802
01:23:09,151 --> 01:23:10,569
Let's not tag each other.

1803
01:23:10,652 --> 01:23:11,695
One of us could be in danger.

1804
01:23:11,778 --> 01:23:13,739
For example, if I'm in first or second,

1805
01:23:13,822 --> 01:23:15,657
and you're in third or fourth, you use it.

1806
01:23:15,741 --> 01:23:17,993
But if you're in the top two, I'll use it.

1807
01:23:18,827 --> 01:23:20,787
-Sounds good.
-Do you want to hold onto the card?

1808
01:23:22,539 --> 01:23:23,540
Okay, I'll hold onto it.

1809
01:23:23,624 --> 01:23:26,668
Okay, then we're teaming up for today.

1810
01:23:26,752 --> 01:23:28,545
-Let's work together and share.
-[Horseking] Okay.

1811
01:23:28,629 --> 01:23:30,464
-[excitedly] This is awesome.
-[Jaegyun giggles]

1812
01:23:30,923 --> 01:23:33,133
He said, "Do you want to keep it?"

1813
01:23:33,217 --> 01:23:36,386
So I was like, "Yes! Thank you,"
and put it in my pocket.

1814
01:23:36,470 --> 01:23:38,972
Jaegyun was the one who found the door.

1815
01:23:39,056 --> 01:23:41,350
Of course, I was by his side, helping him.

1816
01:23:41,433 --> 01:23:44,478
So he deserves to keep it first.

1817
01:23:44,561 --> 01:23:45,562
If you're in first or second,

1818
01:23:45,646 --> 01:23:47,481
-give it to me when you hide.
-[Jaegyun] Okay.

1819
01:23:50,192 --> 01:23:51,985
-[Horseking] This is so hard.
-[Jaegyun] Yeah.

1820
01:23:54,780 --> 01:23:56,782
[♪ stealthy music playing]

1821
01:24:04,873 --> 01:24:07,668
[huffs] Where are they?

1822
01:24:15,801 --> 01:24:17,177
SOMEONE HAS USED THE BLACK CARD

1823
01:24:17,261 --> 01:24:18,387
[Sanghyun] Black Card?

1824
01:24:18,470 --> 01:24:20,389
This is the first time
I'm hearing about it.

1825
01:24:21,014 --> 01:24:22,099
"The Black Card"?

1826
01:24:22,724 --> 01:24:23,725
What is that?

1827
01:24:24,768 --> 01:24:25,978
[Dail] What's the Black Card?

1828
01:24:27,688 --> 01:24:28,772
What?

1829
01:24:29,523 --> 01:24:31,066
[whispering] The Black Card was used?

1830
01:24:31,149 --> 01:24:32,442
The Black Card?

1831
01:24:32,526 --> 01:24:33,860
Uh...

1832
01:24:33,944 --> 01:24:36,572
I got the message
that the Black Card had been used.

1833
01:24:37,948 --> 01:24:40,284
What? Jaegyun used it already?

1834
01:24:41,827 --> 01:24:43,662
-[Horseking] Jaegyun.
-You scared me.

1835
01:24:43,745 --> 01:24:45,539
[Horseking] Jaegyun,
you didn't use the Black Card, did you?

1836
01:24:46,081 --> 01:24:47,958
[Jaegyun] I didn't.

1837
01:24:48,041 --> 01:24:49,167
I saw the message and...

1838
01:24:49,251 --> 01:24:51,837
[Horseking] The thing is,
the Black Card was hidden so well.

1839
01:24:51,920 --> 01:24:53,171
How could someone have it?

1840
01:24:53,255 --> 01:24:55,841
My mind went totally blank then.

1841
01:24:56,967 --> 01:25:00,053
Who could it be? Then, it hit me.
"It's got to be the Seeker."

1842
01:25:00,679 --> 01:25:02,681
This has to be the Seeker's perk.

1843
01:25:02,764 --> 01:25:04,099
[♪ tense music playing]

1844
01:25:06,685 --> 01:25:10,689
[dealer] You've submitted the Black Card.
It is now activated for use.

1845
01:25:11,440 --> 01:25:13,442
[♪ music fades]

1846
01:25:15,861 --> 01:25:17,863
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

1847
01:25:17,946 --> 01:25:19,489
BLACK CARD
ALLOWS YOU TO TAG ANY COLOR

1848
01:25:19,573 --> 01:25:21,283
[host] The Black Card has been activated.

1849
01:25:22,200 --> 01:25:25,162
[Ddolddol] I can tag anyone I want.
I'll get them all.

1850
01:25:26,330 --> 01:25:28,999
[host] ZZONE,
your two-minute isolation is complete.

1851
01:25:29,708 --> 01:25:31,001
[ZZONE] I'm going to get my revenge.

1852
01:25:31,543 --> 01:25:33,253
[Dail] She's coming up as a White Card.

1853
01:25:33,337 --> 01:25:34,796
She's a White Card, so she'll chase us.

1854
01:25:34,880 --> 01:25:36,632
-[Junseo] A White Card?
-We'd better hide.

1855
01:25:36,715 --> 01:25:38,175
[Junseo] What?

1856
01:25:38,258 --> 01:25:41,303
I have to avoid White Cards.
I don't even know what Black Cards are.

1857
01:25:41,386 --> 01:25:44,222
[Dail] They have the Black Card,
which can take anyone out.

1858
01:25:44,306 --> 01:25:45,307
[Jaegyun screams]

1859
01:25:45,390 --> 01:25:46,892
The Black Card. This is ridiculous.

1860
01:25:46,975 --> 01:25:48,810
[Horseking] I knew getting caught
meant I'd be done for.

1861
01:25:48,894 --> 01:25:50,354
[Dail groaning] God damn it.

1862
01:25:50,896 --> 01:25:52,272
[Sanghyun screams]

1863
01:25:54,399 --> 01:25:55,692
[sighs]

1864
01:25:56,401 --> 01:25:58,070
[Horseking groans] I was so annoyed.

1865
01:25:58,737 --> 01:25:59,738
[Ddolddol murmurs] Where did they go?

1866
01:25:59,821 --> 01:26:02,366
I'm going to take first place,
make it to the finals,

1867
01:26:03,659 --> 01:26:05,243
and take everyone out.

1868
01:26:05,327 --> 01:26:07,329
[♪ ominous music playing]

1869
01:26:27,432 --> 01:26:29,434
Translated by Youji Kim
